1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,916
[reporter 1] <i>Two people have been</i>
<i>found dead at a motel in Sinaloa.</i>

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,166
[reporter 2] <i>Last night, forces clashed</i>

3
00:00:11,250 --> 00:00:13,916
<i>as a military operation</i>
<i>confronted cartel members.</i>

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,000
[indistinct overlapping voices]

5
00:00:21,250 --> 00:00:23,500
[reporter 3] <i>Police have successfully</i>
<i>captured and arrested</i>

6
00:00:23,583 --> 00:00:26,541
<i>three local cartel members,</i>
<i>all suspected to have been involved…</i>

7
00:00:27,708 --> 00:00:29,916
[reporter 4] …<i>of the crimes</i>
<i>attributed to Iván Gastélum,</i>

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,750
<i>who might better be known</i>
<i>as his alias, El Cholo.</i>

9
00:00:32,833 --> 00:00:36,333
[reporter 5] <i>…deployed the military</i>
<i>all across the country.</i>

10
00:00:36,416 --> 00:00:37,500
<i>The deployment signals…</i>

11
00:00:37,583 --> 00:00:40,791
[reporter 6] <i>A tribute was held</i>
<i>to honor all of the brave men and women</i>

12
00:00:40,875 --> 00:00:43,500
<i>who have lost their lives</i>
<i>in the line of duty.</i>

13
00:00:43,583 --> 00:00:46,208
[reporter 7] <i>We will always</i>
<i>remember their sacrifices.</i>

14
00:00:46,291 --> 00:00:49,916
[reporter 8] <i>The military seek to strike</i>
<i>a devastating blow to the cartel</i>

15
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:51,958
<i>with the loss of one of their leaders.</i>

16
00:00:52,041 --> 00:00:53,958
[man] I know it's about to be a bloodbath.

17
00:00:54,041 --> 00:00:56,208
[upbeat music playing]

18
00:00:59,083 --> 00:01:01,375
[ominous music playing]

19
00:01:01,916 --> 00:01:05,416
{\an8}BASED ON AN ARTICLE BY
HÉCTOR DE MAULEÓN

20
00:01:06,166 --> 00:01:08,583
[cop 1] <i>Requesting any additional units</i>
<i>in the area.</i>

21
00:01:08,666 --> 00:01:10,875
-[cop 2] <i>Unit Two, en route.</i>
-[cop 3] <i>Unit Six, en route.</i>

22
00:01:10,958 --> 00:01:12,583
[indistinct Spanish dialogue]

23
00:01:15,291 --> 00:01:18,208
{\an8}Put both hands on the table right now!
Hey. Don't be an idiot.

24
00:01:18,291 --> 00:01:19,625
[echoing] <i>Don't be an idiot.</i>

25
00:01:19,708 --> 00:01:21,916
[indistinct Spanish dialogue]

26
00:01:28,833 --> 00:01:29,791
[gunshot]

27
00:01:29,875 --> 00:01:31,875
[breathes heavily]

28
00:01:33,875 --> 00:01:37,000
FACING EL CHAPO

29
00:01:37,083 --> 00:01:39,833
BASED ON TRUE EVENTS

30
00:01:45,458 --> 00:01:49,125
{\an8}JANUARY 6TH, 2016 7:00 AM
LOS MOCHIS, SINALOA

31
00:01:50,833 --> 00:01:52,250
[man sighs]

32
00:01:56,041 --> 00:01:57,250
[girl] Stop it!

33
00:01:57,750 --> 00:01:58,625
[giggles]

34
00:01:59,583 --> 00:02:00,583
Elízabeth!

35
00:02:01,208 --> 00:02:03,958
Elízabeth! Don't ignore me
when I talk to you.

36
00:02:04,041 --> 00:02:05,791
Stop it now, okay?

37
00:02:05,875 --> 00:02:08,416
-Here's your uniform and coffee, honey.
-You're the best. Thanks.

38
00:02:08,916 --> 00:02:11,333
How come you don't buy them
more appropriate toys?

39
00:02:11,416 --> 00:02:12,666
Like Barneys or Barbies.

40
00:02:12,750 --> 00:02:14,666
I would never buy them
those ridiculous toys.

41
00:02:14,750 --> 00:02:16,541
It's from Carlitos, Papa.

42
00:02:16,625 --> 00:02:18,208
Course it was. Give me a break.

43
00:02:18,291 --> 00:02:20,875
Hey! Enough!
Will you stop shooting and sit?!

44
00:02:20,958 --> 00:02:22,458
[woman 1] Listen to your dad.

45
00:02:22,541 --> 00:02:25,666
-Eat all your eggs and beans, okay?
-When are you going to buy us a computer?

46
00:02:25,750 --> 00:02:29,125
Mom said we might actually quiet down
because it would keep us busy.

47
00:02:29,208 --> 00:02:30,541
[man] Jeez.

48
00:02:32,708 --> 00:02:35,500
-Do you want me to take this one?
-[sighs]

49
00:02:35,583 --> 00:02:38,041
You remember everything, Joana?
And what did I tell you?

50
00:02:38,125 --> 00:02:40,708
That your papa will buy you a computer
as soon as he can.

51
00:02:40,791 --> 00:02:44,166
Let me ask you two something.
Do you guys think you deserve a computer?

52
00:02:44,250 --> 00:02:47,041
You keep bothering your sister.
And you, have you done your homework?

53
00:02:47,125 --> 00:02:48,208
[Elízabeth] Yes!

54
00:02:48,291 --> 00:02:50,458
-[man] What do you mean, "yes"?
-Well, no.

55
00:02:50,541 --> 00:02:52,208
-[giggles]
-[man] Mm. [chuckles]

56
00:02:52,291 --> 00:02:55,458
But, Dad, I get good grades
and I never ask for anything.

57
00:02:55,541 --> 00:02:56,916
-[man] Well--
-Morning!

58
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:58,458
Okay, I'll think about it.

59
00:02:58,541 --> 00:03:02,291
-Come on in. Do you want a coffee, or--
-We don't have time. We're late!

60
00:03:02,375 --> 00:03:04,333
Okay, come on, girls.
This is what you get,

61
00:03:04,416 --> 00:03:06,916
'cause you guys kept fooling around
and ran out of time!

62
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:08,958
-[man] Listen to your mom.
-See you later, Arturo.

63
00:03:09,041 --> 00:03:10,791
[woman 2] Let's go! Run, run, run!

64
00:03:10,875 --> 00:03:12,750
[woman 1] Sorry, sweetie.
May God be with you.

65
00:03:12,833 --> 00:03:14,958
-[woman 2] We're blessed! We have to go.
-[woman 1] Bye.

66
00:03:15,041 --> 00:03:16,833
-[woman 2] Bye!
-Thanks for helping us out.

67
00:03:21,583 --> 00:03:22,625
[sighs]

68
00:03:23,291 --> 00:03:25,375
Hey, Liz is a little troublemaker, huh?

69
00:03:25,458 --> 00:03:27,708
We need to watch what we say
because she's getting clever.

70
00:03:27,791 --> 00:03:29,125
-Yeah, I know.
-Mm-hmm.

71
00:03:29,791 --> 00:03:31,208
Come eat. Aren't you hungry?

72
00:03:31,958 --> 00:03:33,125
No appetite.

73
00:03:36,250 --> 00:03:37,708
Are you feeling okay?

74
00:03:38,625 --> 00:03:40,708
No. To be honest, I haven't been great.

75
00:03:46,333 --> 00:03:47,791
What's wrong, honey?

76
00:03:48,541 --> 00:03:51,291
Is it your head? Your stomach?
What's bothering you?

77
00:03:54,083 --> 00:03:55,208
[woman] I'm pregnant.

78
00:04:04,291 --> 00:04:05,750
I'm pregnant, Arturo.

79
00:04:07,291 --> 00:04:10,500
[somber music sting]

80
00:04:11,875 --> 00:04:15,416
-You're not joking, are you?
-And why would I joke about this?

81
00:04:18,666 --> 00:04:20,166
Another daughter?

82
00:04:20,666 --> 00:04:21,750
Or maybe a son?

83
00:04:21,833 --> 00:04:23,416
[Arturo] Holy shit.

84
00:04:26,083 --> 00:04:28,041
I thought you were taking the pill.

85
00:04:33,500 --> 00:04:35,291
Of course I was, Arturo.

86
00:04:35,375 --> 00:04:37,875
I just forgot a couple of days.
That's all.

87
00:04:44,708 --> 00:04:45,958
[uneasy music playing]

88
00:04:46,041 --> 00:04:47,583
I looked at our budget again,

89
00:04:47,666 --> 00:04:50,833
and with my salary, we should be fine.

90
00:04:53,291 --> 00:04:56,458
We're paying for the house, though.
We're paying for the car.

91
00:04:56,541 --> 00:05:00,375
Not to mention all the girls' needs.
Sweetheart, we're barely staying afloat.

92
00:05:01,291 --> 00:05:02,291
-I just--
-Well…

93
00:05:03,833 --> 00:05:05,583
We won't keep it if it's too much trouble.

94
00:05:05,666 --> 00:05:08,000
[sighs] But that's not
what I want us to do.

95
00:05:08,500 --> 00:05:11,000
I just want to be on the same page,
'cause we're having the baby.

96
00:05:11,083 --> 00:05:13,041
I'll go to Valladares
and ask for the night shift.

97
00:05:13,125 --> 00:05:16,875
Not the night shift, Arturo.
It's way more dangerous, honey.

98
00:05:16,958 --> 00:05:18,333
Then what the hell do I do?

99
00:05:18,416 --> 00:05:21,250
Yes, the night shift will be a bitch,
but I'll get used to it.

100
00:05:21,333 --> 00:05:23,791
But what we can't get used to
is not eating.

101
00:05:26,416 --> 00:05:29,208
Well, I'd rather be poor than a widow. Hm?

102
00:05:31,708 --> 00:05:33,750
[sighs] Oh, sweetheart.

103
00:05:35,291 --> 00:05:36,416
[knocking on door]

104
00:05:36,500 --> 00:05:37,500
[music fades]

105
00:05:38,375 --> 00:05:40,500
Good morning, sir.
Do you have two minutes?

106
00:05:40,583 --> 00:05:42,333
Close the door behind you.

107
00:05:43,708 --> 00:05:44,750
Everything good?

108
00:05:46,541 --> 00:05:49,750
Would it be possible for me
to move over to the night shift?

109
00:05:49,833 --> 00:05:53,208
No can do.
I need you out there during the day.

110
00:05:55,583 --> 00:06:00,833
It's just, well, because you can make more
on the night shift, and, um…

111
00:06:04,750 --> 00:06:06,458
Well, I'm going to be a dad again,

112
00:06:06,541 --> 00:06:08,791
and you know
the expenses that come with that.

113
00:06:09,291 --> 00:06:10,750
You guys are pregnant?

114
00:06:11,875 --> 00:06:12,708
Yeah.

115
00:06:18,250 --> 00:06:19,583
[woman] <i>Hey, what's up, girl?</i>

116
00:06:20,333 --> 00:06:22,625
I just picked up
the baby clothes from Vicky.

117
00:06:24,291 --> 00:06:25,333
Are you okay?

118
00:06:25,958 --> 00:06:28,125
Yeah, don't worry. I'm fine.

119
00:06:28,208 --> 00:06:30,750
I can hold onto these
if you haven't told your husband yet.

120
00:06:33,291 --> 00:06:34,458
I broke the news today.

121
00:06:36,375 --> 00:06:37,375
And how'd it go?

122
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:40,500
Well, he told me
we'll figure something out.

123
00:06:41,250 --> 00:06:42,791
He wants the night shift, but

124
00:06:43,625 --> 00:06:45,583
it's been dangerous lately, you know?

125
00:06:47,333 --> 00:06:53,083
FEDERAL POLICE

126
00:06:53,166 --> 00:06:54,333
[Valladares] Carmona.

127
00:06:55,291 --> 00:06:56,666
[Arturo] Yes, Commissioner.

128
00:06:56,750 --> 00:06:59,833
I've just been told we're having
an officer transfer from Arteaga.

129
00:06:59,916 --> 00:07:02,375
-Nuevo León?
-Michoacán.

130
00:07:02,875 --> 00:07:06,083
-It's been a little crazy over there, no?
-So you heard that too.

131
00:07:06,583 --> 00:07:09,583
His last name is Rosales.
I put him on the night shift

132
00:07:09,666 --> 00:07:12,708
and I wasn't sure
which patrol to assign him to, but now…

133
00:07:12,791 --> 00:07:13,625
[chuckles]

134
00:07:13,708 --> 00:07:16,416
-Timing worked out perfectly, didn't it?
-Sure.

135
00:07:16,500 --> 00:07:18,708
That baby must be
a lucky charm for you, Arturo.

136
00:07:18,791 --> 00:07:21,333
Well, I'll need it. [chuckles]

137
00:07:21,916 --> 00:07:23,583
Hey, listen, Arturo.

138
00:07:24,083 --> 00:07:27,250
Make sure you watch this guy closely.
We don't know what he's like.

139
00:07:27,333 --> 00:07:28,708
Of course. I'll keep an eye on him.

140
00:07:28,791 --> 00:07:32,791
Good. Okay. I hope you're ready
for your double shift tonight.

141
00:07:32,875 --> 00:07:34,208
-Thanks again.
-[Valladares] Sure.

142
00:07:35,541 --> 00:07:38,458
[man] So, do you like to ride
with a saddle or bareback?

143
00:07:38,541 --> 00:07:39,875
[woman] I hate saddles.

144
00:07:39,958 --> 00:07:42,708
-[man] Ha. So, bareback?
-[woman] Yes.

145
00:07:42,791 --> 00:07:43,916
[man chuckles] Me too.

146
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:45,708
-[woman] Here you go.
-[man] Thank you.

147
00:07:45,791 --> 00:07:47,916
-[woman] See you next time.
-[man] Thanks, Sandra!

148
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,791
-[woman] Andrea.
-[man] Oh, right, Andrea!

149
00:07:50,875 --> 00:07:51,916
[man chuckles]

150
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:54,000
[pop song playing on radio]

151
00:07:58,708 --> 00:08:00,583
Wait, I have to go now. Bye.

152
00:08:01,083 --> 00:08:03,166
Only way to get through a shift
is strong-ass coffee.

153
00:08:04,666 --> 00:08:05,625
[Arturo] Hm.

154
00:08:06,833 --> 00:08:11,083
We got a long night of driving around
and sitting on our asses. [chuckles]

155
00:08:11,166 --> 00:08:13,166
Is that all you think we do here?

156
00:08:13,250 --> 00:08:14,291
Chill out. Jesus.

157
00:08:14,375 --> 00:08:16,291
-Look, I'm just trying to fit in.
-Hmm.

158
00:08:24,750 --> 00:08:26,708
So, this coffee's strong to you?

159
00:08:29,166 --> 00:08:30,958
Come on. We just got started.

160
00:08:31,041 --> 00:08:33,583
[police radio] …<i>after forensics,</i>
<i>report to Unit 1 to get…</i>

161
00:08:33,666 --> 00:08:35,666
Well, welcome to Mochis.

162
00:08:36,208 --> 00:08:37,583
[Arturo clears throat]

163
00:08:37,666 --> 00:08:38,916
There you go.

164
00:08:39,416 --> 00:08:41,416
[siren wails]

165
00:08:41,500 --> 00:08:43,500
[uneasy music playing]

166
00:08:58,125 --> 00:08:59,166
[music fades]

167
00:09:04,125 --> 00:09:05,291
[Rosales] Check it out.

168
00:09:05,375 --> 00:09:07,333
[Arturo] He's fucked if he's not careful.

169
00:09:07,416 --> 00:09:10,333
[Rosales] Nah. He has
everything under control.

170
00:09:12,708 --> 00:09:14,083
-[car door opens]
-No, hey, wait!

171
00:09:14,916 --> 00:09:16,541
Man, what the fuck?

172
00:09:35,625 --> 00:09:36,625
Good evening.

173
00:09:37,125 --> 00:09:38,000
[man] Evening.

174
00:09:39,041 --> 00:09:41,250
-[Rosales] Everything in order?
-[man] Of course, Officer.

175
00:09:46,500 --> 00:09:49,000
We're done here. Take these guys away.
Get 'em in the truck.

176
00:09:49,083 --> 00:09:51,208
How's it going, Officer? Need any help?

177
00:09:51,791 --> 00:09:55,208
Oh, no, we'll be okay.
As you can see, I've got it under control.

178
00:09:55,291 --> 00:09:57,333
-Excuse me.
-[man] Hurry up.

179
00:09:57,416 --> 00:09:59,583
[tense music playing]

180
00:10:06,708 --> 00:10:07,791
All right, on your feet.

181
00:10:10,541 --> 00:10:12,708
[Rosales] All right, asshole,
show me some ID.

182
00:10:12,791 --> 00:10:16,750
-We just got here from Tijuana yesterday.
-Yeah, this <i>pendejo.</i>

183
00:10:18,708 --> 00:10:19,708
MUNICIPAL POLICE

184
00:10:25,875 --> 00:10:27,750
Hey, I'm keeping my eye on you.

185
00:10:29,791 --> 00:10:31,750
[man] All right,
let's get the fuck out of here.

186
00:10:34,291 --> 00:10:37,375
I'm guessing you've already started
logging the evidence, right?

187
00:10:39,208 --> 00:10:40,333
Standard practice, Officer.

188
00:10:43,250 --> 00:10:45,541
-Hey, don't do--
-Don't do what?

189
00:10:46,458 --> 00:10:48,041
Know your place.

190
00:10:50,583 --> 00:10:52,041
That's a lot of coke.

191
00:10:53,541 --> 00:10:56,958
Just say the word and we'd be happy
to provide an escort to the DA.

192
00:10:59,833 --> 00:11:02,875
Or actually, I should probably
just call in the seizure now.

193
00:11:14,375 --> 00:11:15,625
Okay, Officer.

194
00:11:17,708 --> 00:11:19,000
Let's go to Ahome.

195
00:11:19,875 --> 00:11:20,750
Come on.

196
00:11:24,291 --> 00:11:25,125
Hey!

197
00:11:31,750 --> 00:11:33,125
[Arturo] Can I help you, gentlemen?

198
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:35,375
Is there a problem?

199
00:11:47,083 --> 00:11:48,083
I'm cool.

200
00:11:48,791 --> 00:11:50,000
Then move along.

201
00:11:53,208 --> 00:11:55,208
[engine revs]

202
00:12:14,375 --> 00:12:15,375
Lead the way.

203
00:12:18,333 --> 00:12:20,500
Come on, let's go! Let's move out!

204
00:12:21,833 --> 00:12:22,791
[Arturo sighs]

205
00:12:24,083 --> 00:12:25,041
[Rosales exhales]

206
00:12:27,625 --> 00:12:28,625
[Arturo exhales]

207
00:12:31,083 --> 00:12:32,250
[radio beeps]

208
00:12:32,333 --> 00:12:33,833
Dispatch, do you read?

209
00:12:34,416 --> 00:12:36,208
-Carmona…
-<i>This is dispatch.</i>

210
00:12:36,291 --> 00:12:38,750
Do you realize
you just screwed with that officer's deal?

211
00:12:39,250 --> 00:12:40,250
[music fades]

212
00:12:42,083 --> 00:12:44,625
[lively music playing]

213
00:12:44,708 --> 00:12:47,083
All right. Thanks, Erick.

214
00:12:55,791 --> 00:12:58,625
[woman] <i>I'll be waiting for you</i>
<i>at the motel, okay, baby?</i>

215
00:12:58,708 --> 00:13:00,291
<i>Save some energy for me.</i>

216
00:13:01,791 --> 00:13:02,750
[disconnect tone]

217
00:13:04,750 --> 00:13:05,791
Here you go.

218
00:13:11,833 --> 00:13:13,416
This is supposed to be good?

219
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:16,166
Hm. It's the best in Mochis.

220
00:13:20,166 --> 00:13:21,791
Hey, Rosales.

221
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:25,083
What was all that at the gas station?

222
00:13:26,250 --> 00:13:28,250
[tense music playing]

223
00:13:29,250 --> 00:13:30,416
I'm sorry, what?

224
00:13:31,250 --> 00:13:33,791
What were you showing those assholes
on your phone?

225
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,416
I'm a little confused
about how you do things.

226
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:38,791
What the hell?

227
00:13:40,416 --> 00:13:43,000
Look, asshole, I don't have to explain
how I work to you.

228
00:13:47,625 --> 00:13:48,708
What's your problem?

229
00:13:51,250 --> 00:13:52,916
I don't have a problem.

230
00:13:59,625 --> 00:14:00,625
-[spits]
-[coffee splashes]

231
00:14:03,625 --> 00:14:05,041
What a fucking prick.

232
00:14:11,666 --> 00:14:12,583
[music fades]

233
00:14:15,875 --> 00:14:16,958
[wife] Arturo?

234
00:14:17,041 --> 00:14:17,875
[Arturo] Yeah.

235
00:14:17,958 --> 00:14:19,000
Morning, honey.

236
00:14:19,083 --> 00:14:20,916
-[Arturo] Hey, good morning.
-I missed you.

237
00:14:21,833 --> 00:14:23,250
Want some breakfast? Are you hungry?

238
00:14:23,333 --> 00:14:25,958
I'm exhausted more than anything,
so I'll just eat whatever you have.

239
00:14:26,041 --> 00:14:29,375
There's <i>machaca. </i>And of course
you're tired. How could you not be?

240
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:30,916
[Arturo exhales]

241
00:14:31,583 --> 00:14:33,541
Wow, this is good. Who drew it?

242
00:14:33,625 --> 00:14:35,750
Joana. You know, the artist in the family.

243
00:14:35,833 --> 00:14:37,958
-[Arturo] She's pretty good.
-Here, have some juice too.

244
00:14:38,041 --> 00:14:39,208
[Arturo] Thank you.

245
00:14:40,916 --> 00:14:42,666
Okay, so how was it?

246
00:14:43,166 --> 00:14:46,208
How'd it go with your new partner?
What's he like?

247
00:14:49,666 --> 00:14:51,875
Well, I can't really figure out who he is.

248
00:14:52,458 --> 00:14:53,875
Why? What happened?

249
00:14:56,166 --> 00:14:58,291
I think it's first day-nerves
or something.

250
00:14:58,375 --> 00:14:59,208
[wife] Hm.

251
00:15:00,666 --> 00:15:01,666
How are you doing?

252
00:15:06,083 --> 00:15:06,958
Fine.

253
00:15:08,333 --> 00:15:09,250
Um…

254
00:15:12,041 --> 00:15:16,000
Well, actually, I've been thinking
about what you said.

255
00:15:16,875 --> 00:15:18,541
-And I think that maybe--
-Wait.

256
00:15:18,625 --> 00:15:20,916
-I was just--
-[Arturo] I'm sorry.

257
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:24,041
-[somber music playing]
-To be honest, I was caught off guard.

258
00:15:24,583 --> 00:15:25,625
[inhales]

259
00:15:26,458 --> 00:15:28,958
But one more kid isn't that different,
so I'm sure we'll be okay.

260
00:15:31,458 --> 00:15:32,500
You sure?

261
00:15:32,583 --> 00:15:33,708
[tense music playing]

262
00:15:36,958 --> 00:15:38,333
Completely sure.

263
00:15:43,500 --> 00:15:44,500
[bystanders scream]

264
00:15:47,375 --> 00:15:48,625
[gunshot]

265
00:15:53,958 --> 00:15:55,958
[bystanders scream]

266
00:16:00,500 --> 00:16:02,958
[gulps]

267
00:16:04,625 --> 00:16:05,791
[groans]

268
00:16:08,208 --> 00:16:09,708
[sighs]

269
00:16:11,041 --> 00:16:12,041
[exhales]

270
00:16:14,666 --> 00:16:15,791
[sighs]

271
00:16:15,875 --> 00:16:18,375
Honey, are you okay?

272
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:21,000
What time is it?

273
00:16:22,333 --> 00:16:24,125
It's a little after seven o'clock.

274
00:16:24,208 --> 00:16:27,458
Your partner was early,
so I let him inside. He's on the couch.

275
00:16:30,666 --> 00:16:31,875
Rosales?

276
00:16:40,916 --> 00:16:42,875
[door opens]

277
00:16:45,666 --> 00:16:46,833
[wife] Hey, girls?

278
00:16:49,291 --> 00:16:51,750
-You girls do your homework?
-[both] Yes, Papa.

279
00:16:52,458 --> 00:16:53,666
Wow, I'm proud of both of you.

280
00:16:53,750 --> 00:16:56,541
Now go to your rooms
and get ready for bed. Come on.

281
00:16:56,625 --> 00:16:59,000
-Nice to meet you. And be careful tonight.
-Have a good night.

282
00:16:59,083 --> 00:17:00,500
-[wife] I got it.
-Thanks.

283
00:17:00,583 --> 00:17:02,416
[wife] Come on, girls. Brush your teeth.

284
00:17:03,708 --> 00:17:04,833
Why are you so early?

285
00:17:05,416 --> 00:17:07,708
I, uh… I, uh, got you a peace offering.

286
00:17:16,958 --> 00:17:18,750
Give me ten. I'll be right out.

287
00:17:20,375 --> 00:17:21,958
[Rosales] You have a beautiful family.

288
00:17:22,500 --> 00:17:24,500
[tense music playing]

289
00:17:37,708 --> 00:17:39,708
You know, when I got assigned
to work with you,

290
00:17:40,625 --> 00:17:42,208
you sounded familiar.

291
00:17:43,458 --> 00:17:45,958
But I really couldn't figure out
from where though.

292
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:49,708
And then it finally hit me.

293
00:17:50,208 --> 00:17:51,333
Of course.

294
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:53,583
He's Agent Carmona.

295
00:17:57,208 --> 00:17:58,875
Everyone's heard of your case.

296
00:18:01,500 --> 00:18:03,625
At least you made it out alive
though, right?

297
00:18:04,583 --> 00:18:06,916
Do you know what keeps me up
every fucking night?

298
00:18:10,083 --> 00:18:11,916
Those murdered kids.

299
00:18:14,375 --> 00:18:17,208
I keep thinking of my daughters,
and it fucks with me,

300
00:18:17,291 --> 00:18:20,541
because maybe if I had
just gotten there a little earlier…

301
00:18:22,041 --> 00:18:23,125
I'm fucked up.

302
00:18:23,625 --> 00:18:25,708
You can't keep blaming yourself, <i>cabrón.</i>

303
00:18:26,375 --> 00:18:28,625
It's a miracle he didn't kill you.

304
00:18:29,125 --> 00:18:30,000
Yeah.

305
00:18:33,458 --> 00:18:35,916
How come you wear
such a nice watch to work?

306
00:18:39,458 --> 00:18:41,250
You know a lot about watches?

307
00:18:41,333 --> 00:18:42,416
I know enough.

308
00:18:42,500 --> 00:18:44,625
Because you don't know shit about coffee.

309
00:18:44,708 --> 00:18:45,708
[Arturo chuckles]

310
00:18:49,791 --> 00:18:51,166
[music fades]

311
00:18:58,500 --> 00:18:59,416
[man 1] Commander.

312
00:18:59,500 --> 00:19:01,500
[unsettling music playing]

313
00:19:09,541 --> 00:19:10,750
You there, Bravo?

314
00:19:11,291 --> 00:19:12,500
[man 2] <i>Go ahead, Alpha.</i>

315
00:19:13,166 --> 00:19:15,333
Can you confirm
how many civilians are present?

316
00:19:16,333 --> 00:19:18,833
[man 2] <i>Our cameras</i>
<i>recorded three civilians yesterday,</i>

317
00:19:18,916 --> 00:19:22,041
<i>and no one has left or entered since,</i>
<i>so confirming three.</i>

318
00:19:25,500 --> 00:19:26,541
[man 3] Oh, shit.

319
00:19:27,041 --> 00:19:29,500
Seems like a lot of tacos
for two thugs, right?

320
00:19:29,583 --> 00:19:32,583
Yeah. That's a whole taqueria.

321
00:19:38,208 --> 00:19:39,291
[music fades]

322
00:19:45,333 --> 00:19:46,958
[unsettling music resumes]

323
00:19:47,041 --> 00:19:48,708
<i>Puta madre. </i>[clears throat]

324
00:19:53,833 --> 00:19:54,958
They're armed.

325
00:19:55,458 --> 00:19:58,166
[man 3] Looks like they're the ones
who ordered the tacos, Foco.

326
00:20:02,500 --> 00:20:04,625
-Is El Cholo there?
-[Foco] I'm not sure.

327
00:20:10,750 --> 00:20:13,791
[man 3] Listen, Foco,
if El Cholo's inside,

328
00:20:14,875 --> 00:20:16,458
things are gonna get pretty crazy.

329
00:20:20,500 --> 00:20:22,250
But I won't let us die today.

330
00:20:24,625 --> 00:20:26,125
NAVY

331
00:20:29,041 --> 00:20:30,125
[music fades]

332
00:20:42,333 --> 00:20:43,458
[tense music playing]

333
00:20:43,541 --> 00:20:45,791
-[man 4] <i>Unit 10, go ahead.</i>
-[man 5] <i>Moving in now.</i>

334
00:20:54,166 --> 00:20:55,625
[music fades]

335
00:21:04,125 --> 00:21:05,666
[dramatic music playing]

336
00:21:06,333 --> 00:21:08,500
-Fuck, it's the feds!
-[man 6] Get this shit out of here!

337
00:21:08,583 --> 00:21:11,666
-[man 7] They're already inside!
-[man 3] All right, boys, let's move!

338
00:21:11,750 --> 00:21:13,791
Move it! Come on.

339
00:21:13,875 --> 00:21:15,375
Get in position!

340
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:17,916
Stand clear. Breach the door!

341
00:21:18,750 --> 00:21:20,625
[gunfire]

342
00:21:23,541 --> 00:21:24,750
[gunfire]

343
00:21:26,500 --> 00:21:28,750
Let's go! Push forward!

344
00:21:29,458 --> 00:21:31,208
-Get him out of here!
-Help the corporal!

345
00:21:31,291 --> 00:21:33,625
-[Foco] It's okay, man. I got you.
-[corporal] My arm!

346
00:21:36,083 --> 00:21:37,416
[corporal groans]

347
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:38,958
[man 3] You'll be okay. Hold on.

348
00:21:39,041 --> 00:21:40,333
Deploy grenade!

349
00:21:45,375 --> 00:21:46,375
Weapons hot!

350
00:21:47,083 --> 00:21:49,041
Ready? Let's fucking move!

351
00:21:54,750 --> 00:21:56,166
Keep pressing forward!

352
00:21:56,250 --> 00:21:57,416
Go, go, go!

353
00:21:57,500 --> 00:21:59,958
Clear that room! Check the columns!

354
00:22:03,416 --> 00:22:05,958
Move forward, Foco. Cover the stairs.

355
00:22:07,750 --> 00:22:09,791
Any asshole that tries to run gets shot.

356
00:22:10,291 --> 00:22:12,875
Okay, Foco. <i>Vamos. </i>Advance.

357
00:22:16,250 --> 00:22:17,250
Keep going, Foco!

358
00:22:19,666 --> 00:22:23,625
-[Foco] Come on, boys. Stairway is clear!
-[man 3] Make sure to check that room.

359
00:22:23,708 --> 00:22:25,625
[Foco] Don't fucking move!
Get on the ground!

360
00:22:25,708 --> 00:22:27,583
-[man 2] Hands on the floor!
-[man 8] Don't move!

361
00:22:27,666 --> 00:22:29,541
Keep your fucking hands
where I can see them!

362
00:22:29,625 --> 00:22:33,541
Where the fuck is he? Where's El Cholo?
Fucking talk, <i>cabrón!</i>

363
00:22:33,625 --> 00:22:35,291
[man 3] See if El Cholo's
in the other room!

364
00:22:35,791 --> 00:22:38,041
-[man 2] Stay on the ground!
-[man 3] Take point, Foco!

365
00:22:38,125 --> 00:22:39,375
-On it.
-[man 3] Secure the room!

366
00:22:39,458 --> 00:22:42,041
Put your fucking hands up, <i>cabrón!</i>
On the floor!

367
00:22:44,791 --> 00:22:48,083
Where are you going, <i>cabrón?</i>
Get back down. Come down!

368
00:22:48,166 --> 00:22:50,958
That's right, asshole. Against the wall!

369
00:22:51,958 --> 00:22:53,208
Where did he go?

370
00:22:53,291 --> 00:22:54,750
-What?
-[man 3] Where did El Cholo go?

371
00:22:54,833 --> 00:22:57,333
-I have no idea, I swear!
-Where the fuck is he? Don't lie to me!

372
00:22:57,416 --> 00:22:58,583
[woman] I came with him.

373
00:22:59,708 --> 00:23:01,291
-[man 3] Hey, Cortez!
-[Cortez] Yes, sir!

374
00:23:01,375 --> 00:23:03,416
[man 3] Come here. Secure this area.

375
00:23:03,500 --> 00:23:04,416
[Cortez] Yes, sir!

376
00:23:04,958 --> 00:23:06,375
Don't move. Don't fucking move!

377
00:23:06,458 --> 00:23:07,916
Just like that, asshole!

378
00:23:09,125 --> 00:23:11,000
-[man 2] Hurry up!
-Check everywhere!

379
00:23:11,083 --> 00:23:13,166
Check the closet,
the furniture. Everything!

380
00:23:13,250 --> 00:23:15,333
-[Cortez] Yes, sir!
-Rip this place apart.

381
00:23:15,416 --> 00:23:17,833
He couldn't have fucking vanished.
I know he's here somewhere.

382
00:23:17,916 --> 00:23:19,916
-[panting]
-[tense music playing]

383
00:23:25,916 --> 00:23:28,041
[man 9] It smells like shit.
Damn it, Cholo!

384
00:23:28,125 --> 00:23:29,625
[El Cholo] Just a little further, boss.

385
00:23:31,083 --> 00:23:33,625
[boss] I'm sick
of all these fucking tunnels.

386
00:23:35,041 --> 00:23:38,125
[El Cholo] Suck it up, boss.
You've been through way fucking worse.

387
00:23:40,958 --> 00:23:42,333
[man 1] Vice Admiral, in here.

388
00:23:43,750 --> 00:23:44,750
[music fades]

389
00:23:44,833 --> 00:23:46,375
[vice admiral] What did you find?

390
00:23:46,458 --> 00:23:48,750
[man 1] Thought this might be something.
Check it out.

391
00:23:50,458 --> 00:23:51,916
Everybody, be quiet.

392
00:23:54,916 --> 00:23:56,375
[boss] This is bullshit!

393
00:23:56,458 --> 00:23:58,208
I'm sick of running around
like a fucking rat

394
00:23:58,291 --> 00:24:00,166
through these goddamn tunnels!

395
00:24:03,541 --> 00:24:04,833
[hollow knocking]

396
00:24:08,375 --> 00:24:10,291
[vice admiral] Okay. Get ready, men!

397
00:24:11,458 --> 00:24:13,291
[tense music playing]

398
00:24:13,375 --> 00:24:16,041
-Let's go!
-[Cortez] There's a tunnel, sir!

399
00:24:16,875 --> 00:24:19,458
Sweep the tunnel. See how far it goes.

400
00:24:22,041 --> 00:24:26,541
Damn it. These <i>pendejos</i>
and their fucking tunnels. Come on.

401
00:24:44,541 --> 00:24:46,875
Goddamn it. Corporal?

402
00:24:47,375 --> 00:24:50,500
Tell the admiral we're gonna be
needing more aerial support ASAP.

403
00:24:50,583 --> 00:24:52,500
-[man 10] <i>Copy that, sir.</i>
-Get on it!

404
00:24:54,750 --> 00:24:55,916
Any news?

405
00:24:56,000 --> 00:24:59,875
Unit 2 has just returned. They had
to turn back because of the water level.

406
00:25:00,708 --> 00:25:03,541
-We think it leads to the sewage system.
<i>-Puta madre.</i>

407
00:25:04,833 --> 00:25:07,958
If El Cholo hasn't drowned already,
he'll come out of a manhole.

408
00:25:10,416 --> 00:25:11,708
-Foco.
-Commander.

409
00:25:11,791 --> 00:25:15,625
Get everyone ready. We're leaving.
But leave one unit here just in case.

410
00:25:15,708 --> 00:25:16,833
Yes, sir.

411
00:25:16,916 --> 00:25:20,166
Lieutenant, have the air unit report to us
with anything suspicious.

412
00:25:20,250 --> 00:25:22,291
-Let's clear out, gentlemen!
-[men] Yes, sir.

413
00:25:22,375 --> 00:25:23,708
[man 2] Let's go, marines!

414
00:25:27,375 --> 00:25:28,416
[music stops]

415
00:25:31,916 --> 00:25:33,916
[helicopter blades whirring]

416
00:25:39,708 --> 00:25:42,166
Who is that? Army or the marines?

417
00:25:42,708 --> 00:25:43,791
Not sure.

418
00:25:45,375 --> 00:25:48,458
I just wanna get through this shift
'cause I'm getting some tonight.

419
00:25:50,083 --> 00:25:51,916
Don't you mean this morning?

420
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:52,958
[siren wails]

421
00:25:59,000 --> 00:26:00,458
-Morning.
-[Valladares] Morning, boys.

422
00:26:00,541 --> 00:26:01,958
Did you see the helicopters?

423
00:26:02,041 --> 00:26:05,041
We heard them flying over us,
but what are they doing right now?

424
00:26:05,541 --> 00:26:09,708
The Navy was just involved in a clash,
but they haven't told us who it was with.

425
00:26:10,333 --> 00:26:13,208
And they asked us to make sure
all of our units stand by

426
00:26:13,291 --> 00:26:14,416
and hold their positions.

427
00:26:14,916 --> 00:26:16,000
Copy that.

428
00:26:16,083 --> 00:26:18,083
So stay here
and keep watching the freeway.

429
00:26:18,166 --> 00:26:19,666
-Okay?
-We'll keep a lookout, sir.

430
00:26:23,583 --> 00:26:25,291
-[car door closes]
-[engine starts]

431
00:26:25,375 --> 00:26:26,333
Adios!

432
00:26:27,875 --> 00:26:29,958
This shit just keeps getting worse

433
00:26:30,958 --> 00:26:31,791
[scoffs]

434
00:26:33,708 --> 00:26:35,916
Looks like you might not get some at all.

435
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:37,291
Shut up, Carmona!

436
00:26:37,375 --> 00:26:40,500
You should probably just cancel
with the lucky girl now.

437
00:26:42,666 --> 00:26:44,250
Or lucky guy. I don't judge.

438
00:26:45,625 --> 00:26:47,375
Yeah, you wish, <i>cabrón.</i>

439
00:26:49,375 --> 00:26:51,000
I have a whole roster of girls, you know?

440
00:26:51,083 --> 00:26:53,458
-[lively music plays on radio]
-<i>Chinga su madre!</i>

441
00:26:59,208 --> 00:27:01,750
[in Spanish] ♪ <i>In Reynosa, Tamaulipas </i>♪

442
00:27:01,833 --> 00:27:04,541
♪ <i>Men are determined </i>♪

443
00:27:04,625 --> 00:27:07,333
♪ <i>That's why we remember them </i>♪

444
00:27:07,416 --> 00:27:09,958
♪ <i>By singing their ballads </i>♪

445
00:27:10,041 --> 00:27:13,958
♪ <i>There in Zacatecas, they killed </i>♪

446
00:27:14,041 --> 00:27:19,666
♪ <i>A federal highway agent </i>♪

447
00:27:21,416 --> 00:27:24,958
[in English] Could you be more basic with
your fucking choice in music, Carmona?

448
00:27:25,833 --> 00:27:27,791
"El Federal de Caminos," really?

449
00:27:27,875 --> 00:27:29,208
What the fuck do you listen to?

450
00:27:29,291 --> 00:27:31,250
I listen to real music, <i>cabrón!</i>

451
00:27:31,750 --> 00:27:34,166
-Los Ángeles Negros, for example.
-[laughs]

452
00:27:34,250 --> 00:27:35,541
[boss] Where the fuck are we?

453
00:27:35,625 --> 00:27:37,958
-[El Cholo] Just a little further.
-[boss] Cholo, goddamn it.

454
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:45,916
["El Federal de Caminos"
continues on radio]

455
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:47,458
-Hey, Carmona.
-What?

456
00:27:49,166 --> 00:27:50,458
Does this area get pretty hot?

457
00:27:52,458 --> 00:27:55,083
Well, like anywhere,
it can get a little hot.

458
00:27:55,166 --> 00:27:57,708
Usually, it's normal.
Right now, it's calm.

459
00:27:58,666 --> 00:27:59,875
You

460
00:28:00,666 --> 00:28:02,000
been paid off ever?

461
00:28:05,708 --> 00:28:06,875
Not me, no.

462
00:28:08,625 --> 00:28:10,125
[tense music playing]

463
00:28:28,125 --> 00:28:29,666
[strains]

464
00:28:30,875 --> 00:28:31,958
[boss groans]

465
00:28:36,333 --> 00:28:37,666
[horn honks]

466
00:28:37,750 --> 00:28:39,500
-[boss] Stop the car.
-[El Cholo] Pull over!

467
00:28:39,583 --> 00:28:42,125
[boss] Get out of the fucking car.
Hurry up. Get out!

468
00:28:42,208 --> 00:28:43,708
-Out of the car!
-[woman] Okay.

469
00:28:43,791 --> 00:28:46,333
-[boss] Shut up!
-[woman] Okay. Please, I'm getting out.

470
00:28:46,416 --> 00:28:47,750
[El Cholo] We don't have all day!

471
00:28:47,833 --> 00:28:49,375
-[woman] We have to go.
-[boss] Let's go!

472
00:28:50,625 --> 00:28:52,541
[tires squeal]

473
00:28:53,041 --> 00:28:55,333
-Are you okay?
-We're okay. He's gone.

474
00:28:55,416 --> 00:28:56,375
Oh God.

475
00:28:56,458 --> 00:28:57,583
[child cries]

476
00:28:57,666 --> 00:28:59,416
-We're okay, sweetheart.
-It's over now.

477
00:28:59,916 --> 00:29:01,750
[tense music playing]

478
00:29:13,750 --> 00:29:15,208
Where's the ambulance?

479
00:29:15,291 --> 00:29:17,541
[man 1] <i>Dispatch, do you read?</i>
<i>We've cleared the building.</i>

480
00:29:17,625 --> 00:29:19,166
<i>No snipers confirmed.</i>

481
00:29:19,250 --> 00:29:20,791
-You doing okay?
-[man 1] <i>87-7.</i>

482
00:29:22,750 --> 00:29:26,791
[woman] <i>Be advised. A 56-21 has</i>
<i>been reported on Guillermo Prieto Street.</i>

483
00:29:26,875 --> 00:29:29,375
<i>A 2005 red Ford Focus,</i>

484
00:29:29,458 --> 00:29:32,083
<i>plate Victor, Kilo, Whiskey,</i>
<i>two, zero, six.</i>

485
00:29:32,166 --> 00:29:35,833
<i>I repeat, plates Victor, Kilo, Whiskey,</i>
<i>two, zero, six.</i>

486
00:29:37,250 --> 00:29:39,583
Come on, we've been on the clock
for 12 hours now.

487
00:29:40,083 --> 00:29:40,916
[radio beeps]

488
00:29:42,583 --> 00:29:44,833
-Don't whine.
-[man 2] <i>Unit 3, checking in.</i>

489
00:29:44,916 --> 00:29:46,708
Overtime's always nice.

490
00:29:46,791 --> 00:29:49,541
I don't need extra cash.
I just wanna go get laid.

491
00:29:58,250 --> 00:30:00,666
[man 3] <i>Yeah, I was told to stay here</i>
<i>on Main and Third.</i>

492
00:30:02,125 --> 00:30:03,708
[tense music playing]

493
00:30:03,791 --> 00:30:06,208
Hey. Isn't that the car that was stolen?

494
00:30:06,791 --> 00:30:07,833
Looks like it.

495
00:30:13,791 --> 00:30:15,166
Unit 18, beginning pursuit.

496
00:30:15,250 --> 00:30:17,250
[siren wails]

497
00:30:19,666 --> 00:30:22,208
I've got a 55 with a 56, a possible 21.

498
00:30:25,208 --> 00:30:28,166
<i>Pull over to the right</i>
<i>and stop your vehicle immediately.</i>

499
00:30:29,250 --> 00:30:31,000
[tires squeal]

500
00:30:36,208 --> 00:30:37,208
Out of the car!

501
00:30:37,291 --> 00:30:38,333
[El Cholo] Fucking pigs.

502
00:30:38,416 --> 00:30:40,375
[boss] Easy. Relax, Cholo.

503
00:30:45,208 --> 00:30:49,000
What the fuck are you trying to do to us,
<i>cabrónes? </i>What's your commander's name?

504
00:30:49,625 --> 00:30:51,708
-The boss is with me, <i>pendejo!</i>
-Drop your weapons now!

505
00:30:53,125 --> 00:30:54,000
[scoffs]

506
00:30:54,541 --> 00:30:58,000
Maybe your lucky day. Don't dick around.
We gotta get out of here.

507
00:30:58,083 --> 00:31:00,666
-That's enough!
-Drop your weapons now!

508
00:31:06,291 --> 00:31:07,625
Take two steps back.

509
00:31:08,125 --> 00:31:09,625
I said two steps back!

510
00:31:22,291 --> 00:31:24,041
Hey, hands up. Come on!

511
00:31:26,250 --> 00:31:27,250
Put those on.

512
00:31:29,083 --> 00:31:30,041
Happy, <i>cabrón?</i>

513
00:31:31,250 --> 00:31:32,250
[Rosales] Come here.

514
00:31:36,833 --> 00:31:38,916
That's it. Don't move.

515
00:31:49,375 --> 00:31:50,416
Do you know who I am?

516
00:32:05,125 --> 00:32:07,875
Uh, yeah, I do.

517
00:32:12,666 --> 00:32:14,500
Now please step out of the vehicle.

518
00:32:27,666 --> 00:32:32,166
Calm down, man. Let's fix this.
We need you to take us to Che Ríos.

519
00:32:32,250 --> 00:32:33,416
Not another word.

520
00:32:42,250 --> 00:32:43,166
Turn around!

521
00:32:44,708 --> 00:32:47,208
Come with me to the patrol car.

522
00:32:48,791 --> 00:32:50,000
Come on.

523
00:32:50,791 --> 00:32:51,625
You too.

524
00:32:52,666 --> 00:32:54,250
<i>Andale, cabrón! </i>Move it!

525
00:32:59,166 --> 00:33:00,000
Walk.

526
00:33:07,166 --> 00:33:08,125
Get in.

527
00:33:09,333 --> 00:33:10,666
Come on, get in.

528
00:33:17,000 --> 00:33:18,250
Carmona.

529
00:33:21,000 --> 00:33:24,833
[man on radio] <i>Unit 20 reporting in.</i>
<i>We're back on patrol now. Over.</i>

530
00:33:34,291 --> 00:33:36,000
-[El Cholo] Taking a photo?
-Shut your mouth!

531
00:33:36,083 --> 00:33:37,541
[El Cholo] Fuck you, pig!

532
00:33:38,041 --> 00:33:40,833
-I have to cuff you. It's protocol.
-[boss] Fucking bullshit.

533
00:33:50,000 --> 00:33:50,958
[car door closes]

534
00:33:58,750 --> 00:33:59,708
Fuck.

535
00:34:05,250 --> 00:34:07,416
[cell phone dialing]

536
00:34:10,541 --> 00:34:12,083
[cell phone beeping]

537
00:34:12,166 --> 00:34:13,375
Goddamn it.

538
00:34:14,625 --> 00:34:16,375
What are you doing, <i>cabrón?</i>

539
00:34:17,458 --> 00:34:18,708
Why'd you take that photo?

540
00:34:19,666 --> 00:34:22,875
If you get caught with this,
we'll be shit out of luck.

541
00:34:24,416 --> 00:34:27,041
-Whose fucking side are you on?
-The side where I live, <i>cabrón!</i>

542
00:34:27,833 --> 00:34:29,833
Fuck, just let me think.
Just let me think!

543
00:34:32,083 --> 00:34:34,208
What happened last time
you stuck to protocol?

544
00:34:35,583 --> 00:34:37,083
Innocent people were gunned down.

545
00:34:37,791 --> 00:34:39,083
How dare you say that shit to me?

546
00:34:40,083 --> 00:34:42,833
That fucking photo might save our lives.
Yours and mine, asshole.

547
00:34:43,416 --> 00:34:45,125
It's El Chapo Guzmán, <i>cabrón!</i>

548
00:34:47,916 --> 00:34:49,083
You know what I think?

549
00:34:49,166 --> 00:34:51,875
We should do nothing,
and let 'em drive away.

550
00:34:54,166 --> 00:34:55,166
Carmona…

551
00:34:59,625 --> 00:35:01,083
I don't wanna die today.

552
00:35:06,791 --> 00:35:08,416
And I think you feel the same.

553
00:35:09,916 --> 00:35:11,375
Let's fucking live.

554
00:35:15,833 --> 00:35:17,666
They've already seen our faces.

555
00:35:18,500 --> 00:35:20,333
And they've seen our patrol car number.

556
00:35:22,958 --> 00:35:25,416
We let them go and we're fucked.

557
00:35:27,416 --> 00:35:28,916
And if we take them to where they want…

558
00:35:29,583 --> 00:35:31,416
We'll be fucked either way then.

559
00:35:33,166 --> 00:35:34,958
Well, we can't stay here.

560
00:35:35,583 --> 00:35:38,333
If we don't leave soon,
his men will find us and kill us.

561
00:35:39,291 --> 00:35:41,125
-Carmona…
-Yeah?

562
00:35:41,208 --> 00:35:42,708
We're already dead, <i>cabrón.</i>

563
00:35:43,791 --> 00:35:45,041
Not even God

564
00:35:46,041 --> 00:35:47,333
can protect us.

565
00:35:49,208 --> 00:35:50,916
We'll protect each other, <i>cabrón.</i>

566
00:36:27,875 --> 00:36:29,250
[music fades]

567
00:36:29,333 --> 00:36:30,250
[sighs]

568
00:36:39,458 --> 00:36:41,458
[tense music playing]

569
00:36:44,041 --> 00:36:44,958
[sighs]

570
00:36:46,041 --> 00:36:47,625
[man 1] Hey, let's go!

571
00:36:48,250 --> 00:36:50,500
What are you lazy fucks
even doing right now?

572
00:36:50,583 --> 00:36:52,916
Listen up! Put that shit out, dumbass.

573
00:36:53,791 --> 00:36:57,375
They tried to take down the boss,
but he was able to escape. Huh?

574
00:36:58,833 --> 00:37:02,291
The fuck are you waiting for?
We gotta find him before the marines do.

575
00:37:02,375 --> 00:37:03,583
[men] Yes, sir!

576
00:37:03,666 --> 00:37:05,458
-All right, <i>vamonos.</i>
-[man 2] Hey, let's go!

577
00:37:06,875 --> 00:37:08,000
-[man 3] Hurry!
-[man 4] Move!

578
00:37:08,083 --> 00:37:11,000
-[man 5] Fucking go! Come on!
-[man 2] In the fucking car!

579
00:37:11,083 --> 00:37:12,083
[man 6] Let's get him.

580
00:37:19,791 --> 00:37:20,666
[music fades]

581
00:37:27,208 --> 00:37:31,125
ARTURO, WHERE ARE YOU? CALL ME, PLEASE

582
00:37:34,500 --> 00:37:35,500
[cell phone buzzes]

583
00:37:43,541 --> 00:37:46,791
Hey, officers. We've wasted
a lot of time, you know?

584
00:37:46,875 --> 00:37:48,416
Let's stop fucking around.

585
00:37:49,416 --> 00:37:51,750
Step on the gas
and I'll tell you where to go.

586
00:37:53,833 --> 00:37:55,291
Cooperate, assholes!

587
00:37:55,375 --> 00:37:56,333
Hey, Cholo!

588
00:37:56,416 --> 00:37:57,458
Fuck you, <i>cabrón!</i>

589
00:37:57,541 --> 00:37:58,833
<i>Puta madre.</i>

590
00:38:06,250 --> 00:38:08,166
[vehicle approaching]

591
00:38:15,083 --> 00:38:15,958
[radio beeps]

592
00:38:16,041 --> 00:38:18,458
Hey, guys? I've got some cops here.

593
00:38:18,541 --> 00:38:20,333
P-F-14-82.

594
00:38:20,416 --> 00:38:23,208
-[man on radio] <i>Anyone with them?</i>
-Yeah. A combo.

595
00:38:27,500 --> 00:38:28,750
[tense music playing]

596
00:38:42,250 --> 00:38:43,375
Fuck me.

597
00:38:50,750 --> 00:38:51,833
Oh shit.

598
00:38:51,916 --> 00:38:54,666
Hey, officers.
Our lookout already saw you.

599
00:38:54,750 --> 00:38:57,000
-This is fucking crazy.
-[El Cholo] But it's not too late.

600
00:38:57,083 --> 00:39:00,250
All you have to do is help me
get the boss to Che Ríos.

601
00:39:02,000 --> 00:39:05,708
Help me deliver him safely, and I promise
your life will completely change.

602
00:39:07,541 --> 00:39:08,750
Come on, <i>cabrónes!</i>

603
00:39:17,166 --> 00:39:19,333
Yeah, they've got the boss in the back.

604
00:39:20,333 --> 00:39:22,500
The boss can give you
as much as you want, okay?

605
00:39:23,541 --> 00:39:26,458
Stop dicking around,
and just say a fucking number!

606
00:39:27,541 --> 00:39:28,958
Come on, <i>pendejos!</i>

607
00:39:29,041 --> 00:39:30,375
Ten million!

608
00:39:31,041 --> 00:39:32,125
For each of you, eh?

609
00:39:33,208 --> 00:39:34,833
Come on, Commander.

610
00:39:42,041 --> 00:39:44,750
No way, man. Come on.
There's no fucking way.

611
00:39:59,791 --> 00:40:00,875
Don't do it.

612
00:40:03,125 --> 00:40:04,083
[gunshots]

613
00:40:20,791 --> 00:40:23,166
-Is he down? Looks like he's down.
-Yeah, he's down.

614
00:40:25,333 --> 00:40:26,416
<i>Puta madre!</i>

615
00:40:28,833 --> 00:40:32,125
-Don't make me repeat myself.
-Come on and take it, <i>pendejos!</i>

616
00:40:32,208 --> 00:40:34,041
I'm gonna remember how many you kill.

617
00:40:49,125 --> 00:40:50,875
[music fades]

618
00:40:54,083 --> 00:40:55,541
You guys never answered.

619
00:40:56,125 --> 00:40:58,083
This is gonna be my final offer.

620
00:40:59,250 --> 00:41:01,041
Fifteen million for each of you.

621
00:41:02,916 --> 00:41:03,875
Think carefully

622
00:41:03,958 --> 00:41:06,875
because a shitload of people
are going to die.

623
00:41:09,333 --> 00:41:11,916
The people who failed
to warn me quickly enough,

624
00:41:12,000 --> 00:41:15,000
the people who didn't shut down
those fucking marines,

625
00:41:15,833 --> 00:41:18,666
and the people who think
they can bring me in like a trophy.

626
00:41:19,166 --> 00:41:20,583
Are you one of those people?

627
00:41:20,666 --> 00:41:22,375
[ominous music playing]

628
00:41:22,458 --> 00:41:23,458
That's up to you.

629
00:41:33,125 --> 00:41:34,375
[inaudible dialogue]

630
00:41:48,375 --> 00:41:49,958
You're going into Las Canteras?

631
00:42:05,666 --> 00:42:06,708
[music fades]

632
00:42:08,125 --> 00:42:09,500
Come in, Magas!

633
00:42:12,125 --> 00:42:13,458
[man] Why are we stopping?

634
00:42:14,333 --> 00:42:15,791
Ah, it's Magas.

635
00:42:17,500 --> 00:42:18,583
What's wrong?

636
00:42:18,666 --> 00:42:19,958
Piojo just called me, sir.

637
00:42:20,458 --> 00:42:23,708
Those cops took out Sky and Hormiga.
What's the move?

638
00:42:25,833 --> 00:42:28,500
-They were the ones on Highway 32?
-[Magas] Yes, boss.

639
00:42:29,791 --> 00:42:30,916
[sighs]

640
00:42:32,333 --> 00:42:33,708
What the hell?

641
00:42:34,583 --> 00:42:35,583
Let's keep going.

642
00:42:35,666 --> 00:42:37,666
[tense music playing]

643
00:42:57,166 --> 00:42:59,583
The fuck do these assholes want?

644
00:43:10,500 --> 00:43:12,000
They really following us?

645
00:43:40,958 --> 00:43:43,500
Ha! Looks like the cavalry's here.

646
00:43:44,541 --> 00:43:47,250
You fucked up for sure. Big time.

647
00:43:47,333 --> 00:43:49,208
Well, you're in the crossfire.

648
00:43:50,125 --> 00:43:53,625
And if they shoot, you're not the ones
with the bulletproof vests.

649
00:43:53,708 --> 00:43:55,083
Better not move, assholes.

650
00:43:57,083 --> 00:43:58,083
[music fades]

651
00:44:02,375 --> 00:44:03,458
Hi.

652
00:44:13,500 --> 00:44:15,458
What the fuck do we do now?

653
00:44:23,666 --> 00:44:25,583
We can't let them get close to the car

654
00:44:27,416 --> 00:44:28,916
or we're seriously fucked.

655
00:44:36,291 --> 00:44:37,500
I have to piss.

656
00:44:37,583 --> 00:44:40,833
No, wait, wait, come on.
You have to be fucking kidding me, <i>cabrón.</i>

657
00:44:44,375 --> 00:44:45,500
Divide and conquer.

658
00:44:47,375 --> 00:44:48,708
Don't let 'em get close.

659
00:44:56,625 --> 00:44:58,625
[tense music playing]

660
00:45:03,833 --> 00:45:05,125
Morning, Commander.

661
00:45:07,625 --> 00:45:08,708
You seem lost.

662
00:45:08,791 --> 00:45:11,000
We'll just fill up and go, okay?

663
00:45:11,583 --> 00:45:15,166
These cops are fucking idiots.
They don't know what they're doing.

664
00:45:16,041 --> 00:45:18,041
-Yeah.
-Gonna get killed.

665
00:45:20,375 --> 00:45:21,666
[whispers] <i>Chinga su madre.</i>

666
00:45:25,208 --> 00:45:28,000
Could you both put away your guns
and show me your permits?

667
00:45:28,083 --> 00:45:29,458
It's just protocol.

668
00:45:30,041 --> 00:45:31,083
You're a funny guy.

669
00:45:31,583 --> 00:45:34,958
[breathes deeply]

670
00:45:37,500 --> 00:45:38,916
We all good here?

671
00:45:44,166 --> 00:45:45,875
Don't be stupid.

672
00:45:45,958 --> 00:45:47,166
Let go.

673
00:45:47,250 --> 00:45:48,541
There we go.

674
00:45:49,041 --> 00:45:50,208
Nice and easy.

675
00:45:55,541 --> 00:45:57,041
[Arturo] Relax, buddy,

676
00:45:58,250 --> 00:46:00,250
unless you wanna set off some fireworks.

677
00:46:01,791 --> 00:46:03,166
What happened?

678
00:46:05,208 --> 00:46:06,916
Why all the violence?

679
00:46:08,625 --> 00:46:12,250
Huh? We're just getting our gas.
We don't want any problems.

680
00:46:19,875 --> 00:46:22,041
Hurry up and leave while you still can.

681
00:46:23,708 --> 00:46:24,708
Good.

682
00:46:31,125 --> 00:46:32,208
Nothing's gonna happen, huh?

683
00:46:45,458 --> 00:46:48,583
-What do I owe you for the gas?
-You don't owe me anything, Officer.

684
00:46:49,750 --> 00:46:50,666
[Rosales] Right.

685
00:47:27,916 --> 00:47:28,875
[music fades]

686
00:47:35,416 --> 00:47:38,041
So, what then? We can take 'em one on one.

687
00:47:42,916 --> 00:47:45,500
If we keep driving in circles
with those <i>cabrónes,</i>

688
00:47:46,041 --> 00:47:47,416
we'll end up dead.

689
00:47:51,750 --> 00:47:53,333
[cell phone dialing]

690
00:47:55,125 --> 00:47:56,458
What are you doing?

691
00:47:57,250 --> 00:47:59,208
Pick up the fucking phone, Valladares.

692
00:48:07,375 --> 00:48:08,541
I'm sending the photo.

693
00:48:11,416 --> 00:48:12,416
Are you sure?

694
00:48:32,541 --> 00:48:34,541
[tense music playing]

695
00:48:37,458 --> 00:48:39,666
What about hiding at Motel del Puerto?

696
00:48:41,458 --> 00:48:42,583
It's close by.

697
00:48:45,375 --> 00:48:46,208
Heh?

698
00:48:46,791 --> 00:48:48,833
Sounds good. All right.

699
00:48:55,000 --> 00:48:57,041
[engine starts]

700
00:49:12,375 --> 00:49:13,875
[music fades]

701
00:49:15,541 --> 00:49:18,458
-You like that?
-[woman] Yeah, it feels so good.

702
00:49:18,541 --> 00:49:20,583
[woman breathes heavily]

703
00:49:20,666 --> 00:49:22,166
What? Did you come?

704
00:49:22,666 --> 00:49:25,625
I can't believe your motel's
gonna help us get out of this mess.

705
00:49:25,708 --> 00:49:27,708
God protects the horny, Carmona.

706
00:49:31,125 --> 00:49:34,208
There has to be a shit ton of lookouts
by now, so we have to stay alert.

707
00:49:34,291 --> 00:49:35,125
[Rosales] Right.

708
00:49:35,208 --> 00:49:36,666
Book a room for us.

709
00:49:37,166 --> 00:49:39,750
I'll move the patrol car to the back
so it's out of view.

710
00:49:40,458 --> 00:49:42,750
You take El Chapo. I'll take El Cholo.

711
00:49:43,333 --> 00:49:44,750
Divide and conquer?

712
00:49:46,083 --> 00:49:47,000
Okay.

713
00:49:47,916 --> 00:49:48,875
Carmona.

714
00:49:50,791 --> 00:49:52,708
The thing with the phone back then?

715
00:49:53,916 --> 00:49:56,916
It's because he asked for the address
of where they were taking his friend.

716
00:49:57,000 --> 00:49:59,916
And since I didn't know,
I looked it up and showed him.

717
00:50:00,416 --> 00:50:01,541
And my watch?

718
00:50:06,625 --> 00:50:08,375
It was a gift from my old man.

719
00:50:09,166 --> 00:50:10,291
On his death bed.

720
00:50:13,458 --> 00:50:14,583
Rosales,

721
00:50:16,166 --> 00:50:17,291
I know who you are.

722
00:50:21,083 --> 00:50:23,291
[upbeat music playing on radio]

723
00:50:23,375 --> 00:50:25,458
-Morning.
-Morning! Um, how can I help?

724
00:50:25,541 --> 00:50:28,250
-[Arturo] How many rooms do you have?
-How many do you need?

725
00:50:34,166 --> 00:50:35,375
We have 60 rooms.

726
00:50:35,458 --> 00:50:36,708
One's all we need.

727
00:50:37,208 --> 00:50:38,083
[music stops]

728
00:50:39,333 --> 00:50:40,333
[car door closes]

729
00:50:42,208 --> 00:50:47,375
Come on, man. Let's strike a deal
now that your partner's inside.

730
00:50:48,541 --> 00:50:49,958
Deliver me to Che Ríos.

731
00:50:50,958 --> 00:50:52,916
It's just one small thing you have to do,

732
00:50:53,000 --> 00:50:55,625
and then you'll be set
for the rest of your life.

733
00:50:55,708 --> 00:50:59,125
Imagine how nice it'll be
to never worry about money again.

734
00:51:00,250 --> 00:51:02,375
And you know what's even better than that?

735
00:51:04,708 --> 00:51:06,333
Your entire family,

736
00:51:07,250 --> 00:51:08,333
including you,

737
00:51:08,833 --> 00:51:10,333
will enter my protection.

738
00:51:11,416 --> 00:51:12,291
I promise.

739
00:51:12,375 --> 00:51:15,416
No one will touch you.
So come on, let's go.

740
00:51:16,416 --> 00:51:17,833
[El Cholo] Take the deal, Officer.

741
00:51:17,916 --> 00:51:20,666
That's the best fucking decision
you'll ever make in your life, <i>cabrón.</i>

742
00:51:23,083 --> 00:51:24,375
I don't know if I can.

743
00:51:24,458 --> 00:51:26,458
Don't think about it. Just start driving.

744
00:51:28,250 --> 00:51:30,250
We got a deal, man.
Hurry up, we're in a rush.

745
00:51:30,333 --> 00:51:32,041
Let's get the fuck out of here, <i>cabrón.</i>

746
00:51:39,083 --> 00:51:40,500
How many are taken?

747
00:51:40,583 --> 00:51:42,541
-[upbeat music playing on radio]
-Only three.

748
00:51:44,250 --> 00:51:45,708
That one, right on the corner.

749
00:51:45,791 --> 00:51:46,875
Number 51.

750
00:51:46,958 --> 00:51:48,166
-It's available?
-[woman] Yeah.

751
00:51:50,708 --> 00:51:52,708
350 pesos for three hours.

752
00:51:54,333 --> 00:51:55,291
[music stops]

753
00:51:55,375 --> 00:51:57,458
Know how long I've been with the police?

754
00:51:59,125 --> 00:52:00,333
Twenty-nine years.

755
00:52:01,375 --> 00:52:04,333
And in my career,
I have seen a whole lot of bullshit.

756
00:52:05,500 --> 00:52:07,958
Especially shit that assholes like you do.

757
00:52:09,166 --> 00:52:10,708
I retire next year.

758
00:52:12,583 --> 00:52:14,375
I've been thinking, you know,

759
00:52:14,875 --> 00:52:18,500
what better gift
than to see you two get what you deserve,

760
00:52:18,583 --> 00:52:19,916
to rot away in a cell?

761
00:52:20,000 --> 00:52:21,125
I'm gonna fucking--

762
00:52:21,208 --> 00:52:23,208
[tense music playing]

763
00:52:23,875 --> 00:52:25,958
[El Chapo] That's enough. Relax, Cholo.

764
00:52:26,041 --> 00:52:29,416
-I'm gonna fucking kill you.
-[Rosales] Sit the fuck down, asshole.

765
00:52:29,916 --> 00:52:31,000
Don't worry.

766
00:52:31,916 --> 00:52:32,916
He'll get his soon.

767
00:52:34,541 --> 00:52:36,208
-[growls softly]
-[knocking on window]

768
00:52:36,291 --> 00:52:38,083
[engine starts]

769
00:53:04,458 --> 00:53:06,375
What do you think
those guys are doing here?

770
00:53:07,208 --> 00:53:08,625
[man] How the fuck should I know?

771
00:53:10,083 --> 00:53:11,166
<i>Puta madre.</i>

772
00:53:17,625 --> 00:53:19,708
[woman] Maybe they're here
to blow off some steam too.

773
00:53:19,791 --> 00:53:20,833
Shh!

774
00:53:25,750 --> 00:53:26,583
Hold on.

775
00:53:30,375 --> 00:53:33,333
-Can you please just spit out a number?
-Okay, come on.

776
00:53:33,416 --> 00:53:34,666
-[El Cholo] Wait, what?
-Get out.

777
00:53:34,750 --> 00:53:37,666
Hey! Where the fuck
are you taking the boss, <i>cabrón?</i>

778
00:53:37,750 --> 00:53:39,333
[man] Holy shit!

779
00:53:39,833 --> 00:53:41,333
There's no fucking way.

780
00:53:41,416 --> 00:53:42,666
[camera clicks]

781
00:53:50,375 --> 00:53:51,416
I can't believe it.

782
00:53:54,125 --> 00:53:55,166
What the fuck?

783
00:53:55,666 --> 00:53:57,291
That asshole kinda looks like…

784
00:53:57,791 --> 00:53:58,875
Like who?

785
00:54:00,125 --> 00:54:00,958
Keep going.

786
00:54:01,041 --> 00:54:03,833
[El Cholo] Put away your fucking gun.
Let's fight like men, motherfucker!

787
00:54:03,916 --> 00:54:06,125
Where the hell's he taking him, <i>cabrón?</i>

788
00:54:12,458 --> 00:54:15,166
[key jangles]

789
00:54:24,125 --> 00:54:25,083
[music fades]

790
00:54:26,333 --> 00:54:27,166
[Arturo] Get in.

791
00:54:37,625 --> 00:54:38,541
Sit down.

792
00:54:39,250 --> 00:54:41,250
[cell phone buzzing and ringing]

793
00:54:41,875 --> 00:54:44,000
INCOMING CALL
ISA

794
00:54:45,541 --> 00:54:46,458
Shit.

795
00:55:01,708 --> 00:55:04,500
-Keep it up, you guys. Good work.
-[man] Yes, sir.

796
00:55:04,583 --> 00:55:05,583
[cell phone buzzes]

797
00:55:21,875 --> 00:55:23,666
[cell phone buzzes and rings]

798
00:55:25,166 --> 00:55:26,500
Now you fucking call me.

799
00:55:27,625 --> 00:55:28,583
Give me a sec.

800
00:55:38,583 --> 00:55:39,416
Morning.

801
00:55:39,500 --> 00:55:41,958
Cut the shit, Carmona.
Who the fuck sent you that photo?

802
00:55:42,041 --> 00:55:43,708
No one did, sir.

803
00:55:45,333 --> 00:55:46,333
I took the photo.

804
00:55:46,416 --> 00:55:47,250
[scoffs]

805
00:55:47,333 --> 00:55:48,625
No way. Where are you?

806
00:55:49,125 --> 00:55:51,916
Well, since you didn't answer,
we had no choice but to lay low

807
00:55:52,000 --> 00:55:53,791
and hide out with him at a motel.

808
00:55:53,875 --> 00:55:57,541
You mean… You mean…
You mean to tell me this is real?

809
00:55:57,625 --> 00:55:59,375
<i>Su puta madre!</i>

810
00:56:01,291 --> 00:56:02,875
I'll send out the photo right away.

811
00:56:02,958 --> 00:56:05,416
Wait! We have to think this through
before we send it.

812
00:56:06,250 --> 00:56:08,541
[Valladares] <i>You're right.</i>
<i>Who can we trust?</i>

813
00:56:09,583 --> 00:56:12,541
I know. Everybody'll get the photo.

814
00:56:12,625 --> 00:56:15,291
<i>My supervisors, the Navy, the Army.</i>

815
00:56:15,375 --> 00:56:18,916
I'll send it to everyone!
Stay right where you are.

816
00:56:19,000 --> 00:56:20,708
Listen to me. Stay put.

817
00:56:20,791 --> 00:56:22,458
<i>And don't talk to anyone, okay?</i>

818
00:56:22,541 --> 00:56:25,750
<i>Every road will be crawling with</i>
<i>those thugs, looking for that bastard.</i>

819
00:56:26,250 --> 00:56:29,916
All right, but you better hurry up
and get here,

820
00:56:30,625 --> 00:56:32,416
because having to stay
with this motherfucker

821
00:56:32,500 --> 00:56:34,166
is like babysitting the devil.

822
00:56:35,208 --> 00:56:36,541
[Valladares] <i>I can only imagine.</i>

823
00:56:36,625 --> 00:56:40,083
<i>Just hang in there, okay? Don't leave</i>
<i>the room, and don't talk to him.</i>

824
00:56:55,958 --> 00:56:57,541
[El Chapo] What's your plan?

825
00:56:57,625 --> 00:56:58,458
[music stops]

826
00:57:03,875 --> 00:57:07,541
I'm not gonna try to run, so can you
please just, uh, take these off me?

827
00:57:09,750 --> 00:57:10,625
[sighs]

828
00:57:14,166 --> 00:57:17,208
Commander, there's something
I wanna ask you.

829
00:57:17,833 --> 00:57:20,250
You and I have nothing to talk about, so

830
00:57:21,375 --> 00:57:23,666
I'm going to ask you
to just stay quiet, please.

831
00:57:27,416 --> 00:57:28,375
[cell phone ringing]

832
00:57:30,875 --> 00:57:32,500
How come you didn't reply to me?

833
00:57:33,541 --> 00:57:35,166
Did you see the fucking photo?

834
00:57:35,250 --> 00:57:36,166
[tense music playing]

835
00:57:36,250 --> 00:57:37,916
Yes, you idiot. It's El Chapo!

836
00:57:38,000 --> 00:57:39,125
Okay, okay, I got it.

837
00:57:39,208 --> 00:57:41,000
Listen, baby, you have to let me know

838
00:57:41,083 --> 00:57:43,250
if any more cops show up,
or take him away.

839
00:57:43,333 --> 00:57:44,458
-Okay.
-[man 1] <i>Thanks.</i>

840
00:57:45,458 --> 00:57:48,041
Hurry the hell up and get us
to Motel del Puerto. The boss is there!

841
00:57:48,125 --> 00:57:51,000
Everyone, fucking head over
to Motel del Puerto.

842
00:57:51,083 --> 00:57:52,375
Motel del Puerto, hurry.

843
00:57:59,875 --> 00:58:02,500
[man 1] I'm about to send you a photo.
Find out who the fuck this is.

844
00:58:02,583 --> 00:58:05,625
I'LL CALL U RIGHT BACK

845
00:58:07,291 --> 00:58:10,750
[man 2] <i>His name is Arturo Carmona,</i>
<i>and he lives in Ahome, Sinaloa.</i>

846
00:58:10,833 --> 00:58:13,083
<i>He's happily married with two kids.</i>

847
00:58:13,166 --> 00:58:15,333
All right, man.
I'll hit you up later, <i>cabrón.</i>

848
00:58:19,583 --> 00:58:21,583
[cell phone dialing]

849
00:58:23,750 --> 00:58:24,916
Guatafuck.

850
00:58:25,000 --> 00:58:29,125
I'm about to send over an address.
A fucking cop lives there, okay?

851
00:58:29,625 --> 00:58:31,666
He has a wife and a couple of kids.

852
00:58:32,166 --> 00:58:33,833
Call me when it's done, eh?

853
00:58:33,916 --> 00:58:35,125
[music fades]

854
00:58:36,625 --> 00:58:38,041
Good morning, Rosita.

855
00:58:38,125 --> 00:58:40,166
Yeah, it's… it's Isaura.

856
00:58:40,666 --> 00:58:42,375
Look, I'm a little worried

857
00:58:42,458 --> 00:58:44,583
because Arturo's shift ended a while ago,

858
00:58:44,666 --> 00:58:47,500
and he hasn't gotten home yet
and won't answer my calls.

859
00:58:51,291 --> 00:58:52,166
[exhales]

860
00:58:52,250 --> 00:58:53,083
[sniffs]

861
00:58:56,583 --> 00:58:58,583
[telephone ringing]

862
00:59:01,541 --> 00:59:02,666
Yeah, what is it?

863
00:59:05,083 --> 00:59:06,125
Put her through.

864
00:59:07,958 --> 00:59:10,708
<i>This is Commissioner Valladares.</i>
<i>How can I help?</i>

865
00:59:10,791 --> 00:59:12,291
M… M… Morning, sir.

866
00:59:12,375 --> 00:59:15,333
This is Isaura. I'm looking for Arturo.
Know where he is?

867
00:59:15,416 --> 00:59:19,375
Arturo is, uh, on special operations
so he'll be late getting home.

868
00:59:19,916 --> 00:59:22,916
Listen, you need to pick up your daughters
from school now and take 'em home.

869
00:59:23,708 --> 00:59:26,833
But is Arturo gonna be okay?
And what do you mean by operation?

870
00:59:26,916 --> 00:59:28,041
[Valladares] <i>Isaura, please,</i>

871
00:59:28,125 --> 00:59:30,791
<i>take the girls home</i>
<i>and wait for Arturo to get there.</i>

872
00:59:30,875 --> 00:59:32,958
If anything goes wrong, call me.

873
00:59:37,333 --> 00:59:38,625
Oh my God.

874
00:59:41,750 --> 00:59:43,833
-Okay.
-[bell rings]

875
00:59:45,750 --> 00:59:46,958
Stay right here.

876
00:59:47,666 --> 00:59:49,250
I'll find out what's going on.

877
00:59:49,750 --> 00:59:51,750
[cell phone buzzing and ringing]

878
01:00:05,708 --> 01:00:06,916
[chuckles softly]

879
01:00:07,000 --> 01:00:09,041
You wife must be worried about you, right?

880
01:00:13,083 --> 01:00:16,458
I'm not in the mood to play your games,
so let's just sit here in silence, okay?

881
01:00:21,833 --> 01:00:24,125
I don't understand what makes you think

882
01:00:24,208 --> 01:00:26,375
that you'll be rewarded
for bringing me in.

883
01:00:26,958 --> 01:00:27,791
Huh?

884
01:00:28,625 --> 01:00:29,708
I already told you.

885
01:00:30,208 --> 01:00:34,416
I got everyone in your whole department
in my goddamn pocket, hombre!

886
01:00:34,500 --> 01:00:36,458
[tense music playing]

887
01:00:36,541 --> 01:00:39,125
When will you stop playing dumb, Officer?

888
01:00:43,500 --> 01:00:46,416
You clearly care a lot
about your family, Carmona.

889
01:00:46,916 --> 01:00:49,208
And you'd probably
do anything for them, no?

890
01:00:50,708 --> 01:00:53,166
-[music fades]
-Everything I do, I do for my children.

891
01:00:54,416 --> 01:00:55,750
Now it's your turn.

892
01:00:56,291 --> 01:00:58,875
You need to do
what you need to do for them.

893
01:01:00,250 --> 01:01:02,791
If you don't accept the offer
I'm willing to give you, my friend,

894
01:01:03,291 --> 01:01:05,041
then someone else will, <i>cabrón.</i>

895
01:01:08,416 --> 01:01:10,875
So it might as well be you.

896
01:01:12,083 --> 01:01:13,708
So let's do it, Officer.

897
01:01:17,333 --> 01:01:18,166
[inhales]

898
01:01:18,250 --> 01:01:20,250
Mm. [mutters]

899
01:01:20,750 --> 01:01:23,125
Officer, can you pass me
a bottle of water?

900
01:01:23,208 --> 01:01:25,166
I'm… I'm really thirsty.

901
01:01:27,541 --> 01:01:30,083
It's just a bottle of water,
for fuck's sake.

902
01:01:40,916 --> 01:01:42,833
[tense music playing]

903
01:01:46,333 --> 01:01:47,541
Don't be an idiot.

904
01:01:48,750 --> 01:01:49,958
You think you're slick?

905
01:01:51,083 --> 01:01:51,916
[music fades]

906
01:01:52,000 --> 01:01:55,000
No. I just wanted to ask you
to open it for me.

907
01:01:56,000 --> 01:01:57,375
Come on, help me out.

908
01:01:58,125 --> 01:01:59,166
Pretty please?

909
01:02:09,666 --> 01:02:10,750
[gun clicks]

910
01:02:15,541 --> 01:02:17,541
[suspenseful music playing]

911
01:02:34,166 --> 01:02:35,291
[music fades]

912
01:02:43,416 --> 01:02:45,250
-[door handle rattles]
-[Arturo] Hey, hey.

913
01:02:46,041 --> 01:02:47,250
Stay there.

914
01:02:56,333 --> 01:02:58,833
[door handle rattles]

915
01:02:59,833 --> 01:03:02,541
-[door handle rattles]
-[tense music playing]

916
01:03:38,416 --> 01:03:39,708
[breathes shakily]

917
01:03:39,791 --> 01:03:42,166
[El Chapo] You're scared
to death, aren't you?

918
01:03:42,750 --> 01:03:46,333
So this is your first time
being in deep shit like this.

919
01:03:47,125 --> 01:03:48,541
<i>Chingada madre!</i>

920
01:03:50,166 --> 01:03:51,125
[music fades]

921
01:03:51,208 --> 01:03:53,500
[Foco] We have units
in these three sectors.

922
01:03:53,583 --> 01:03:54,750
This is where we are.

923
01:03:54,833 --> 01:03:56,750
Thanks to the information
from the sewer company,

924
01:03:56,833 --> 01:03:58,125
every drain is covered now.

925
01:03:58,208 --> 01:03:59,375
[marine] Understood.

926
01:03:59,458 --> 01:04:00,458
[vice admiral sighs]

927
01:04:01,541 --> 01:04:02,958
<i>Puta madre.</i>

928
01:04:03,041 --> 01:04:04,791
What if this fucker slipped away?

929
01:04:06,208 --> 01:04:08,250
He should have
come out of a storm drain by now.

930
01:04:09,916 --> 01:04:11,083
[cell phone chimes]

931
01:04:17,916 --> 01:04:19,916
[suspenseful music playing]

932
01:04:25,125 --> 01:04:26,375
[cell phone rings]

933
01:04:26,458 --> 01:04:27,958
Go ahead, Admiral.

934
01:04:28,041 --> 01:04:29,083
[music fades]

935
01:04:35,666 --> 01:04:36,666
Understood.

936
01:04:37,500 --> 01:04:38,750
[suspenseful music resumes]

937
01:04:38,833 --> 01:04:40,583
-Foco!
-Sir.

938
01:04:42,125 --> 01:04:43,833
The Federal Police have El Cholo.

939
01:04:44,958 --> 01:04:46,750
And look at the prize they got.

940
01:04:50,250 --> 01:04:51,333
It's El Chapo, Commander.

941
01:04:54,750 --> 01:04:55,875
Venado!

942
01:04:58,750 --> 01:05:02,208
Get us the address of Motel del Puerto.
That's where the party's at.

943
01:05:02,291 --> 01:05:04,583
-[Venado] Yes, sir.
-Let's move, everyone! To the motel!

944
01:05:04,666 --> 01:05:06,291
Let's go, marines!

945
01:05:09,041 --> 01:05:11,458
[engine starts]

946
01:05:17,916 --> 01:05:18,791
[music stops]

947
01:05:28,333 --> 01:05:30,708
-[breathing shakily]
-[tense music playing]

948
01:05:36,875 --> 01:05:37,791
[Isaura] Gracias.

949
01:05:43,375 --> 01:05:46,166
-[teacher] May God be with you.
-Thank you.

950
01:05:54,875 --> 01:05:56,500
Hurry up. Get in, get in.

951
01:06:23,708 --> 01:06:25,833
[man 1] Boss! We got heat Incoming.

952
01:06:26,500 --> 01:06:28,375
[man 2] <i>Chingada madre.</i>

953
01:06:34,333 --> 01:06:35,875
-Commander?
-What do you got?

954
01:06:35,958 --> 01:06:38,166
Seems like those assholes
might know where to go too.

955
01:06:41,541 --> 01:06:43,083
Think you're right, Foco.

956
01:06:43,166 --> 01:06:46,208
Hey, boys, you guys
can take care of those marines.

957
01:06:46,291 --> 01:06:48,000
We'll go on ahead to the motel.

958
01:06:52,375 --> 01:06:54,625
[vice admiral] Captain,
however this goes down,

959
01:06:54,708 --> 01:06:56,541
just keep following
anybody who tries to escape.

960
01:06:58,666 --> 01:06:59,583
[tires squeal]

961
01:07:01,250 --> 01:07:03,375
-Split off and chase them down.
-[marine] Yes, sir!

962
01:07:03,458 --> 01:07:07,000
[vice admiral] Don't let them get away!
Step on it, Foco!

963
01:07:08,458 --> 01:07:10,416
Don't lose them, marine. Come on!

964
01:07:10,500 --> 01:07:12,458
We have to catch up to those assholes!

965
01:07:16,250 --> 01:07:17,416
[tires squeal]

966
01:07:17,500 --> 01:07:18,375
[music fades]

967
01:07:18,458 --> 01:07:19,875
Let's dance, <i>cabrónes!</i>

968
01:07:19,958 --> 01:07:21,375
[man 1] Come on, let's go!

969
01:07:21,458 --> 01:07:23,375
[man 2] We're going to fuck you up!

970
01:07:23,458 --> 01:07:24,416
[Magas] Bring it on!

971
01:07:28,666 --> 01:07:31,291
-[Venado] Put the guns down now!
-You first, <i>cabrón!</i>

972
01:07:31,375 --> 01:07:32,750
[Venado] Put them down now!

973
01:07:32,833 --> 01:07:34,625
Hold your ground, <i>cabrónes!</i>

974
01:07:35,250 --> 01:07:36,458
[Venado] Surrender now!

975
01:07:39,750 --> 01:07:43,958
Don't make me fucking say it again.
Everyone, put down your weapons now!

976
01:07:44,458 --> 01:07:45,916
There's nowhere to run.

977
01:07:46,666 --> 01:07:48,041
[man 3] Fuck this!

978
01:07:48,125 --> 01:07:48,958
[man 3 grunts]

979
01:07:49,458 --> 01:07:50,708
Okay, okay!

980
01:07:58,791 --> 01:07:59,750
[Venado] Move in.

981
01:08:01,208 --> 01:08:02,291
Stay alert.

982
01:08:02,791 --> 01:08:04,916
-On the ground!
-[marine 1] Put your hands on the floor!

983
01:08:05,000 --> 01:08:07,708
-[marine 2] Show me your hands!
-[marine 3] Don't fucking try anything.

984
01:08:07,791 --> 01:08:10,416
[Venado] That's it, motherfucker.
Keep your hands on your head.

985
01:08:14,750 --> 01:08:16,666
Uh, h… how are you doing, girls?

986
01:08:16,750 --> 01:08:19,375
What… What did you
take us out of school for, Mama?

987
01:08:21,250 --> 01:08:23,250
[tense music playing]

988
01:08:26,000 --> 01:08:26,833
Come on.

989
01:08:34,791 --> 01:08:35,708
Come here.

990
01:08:39,208 --> 01:08:42,041
Go on. Run. Hurry. Come on, let's go.

991
01:08:42,583 --> 01:08:44,708
Get inside the house. I'll be right there.

992
01:08:55,708 --> 01:08:56,791
[music fades]

993
01:08:59,791 --> 01:09:01,791
[both breathing anxiously]

994
01:09:14,375 --> 01:09:16,958
I didn't get to finish my lunch, Mama.
I'm still hungry!

995
01:09:17,041 --> 01:09:18,333
Oh, sweetie.

996
01:09:18,958 --> 01:09:21,291
Listen, girls, I need you
to go to your rooms

997
01:09:21,375 --> 01:09:23,000
and eat the rest of your lunch there.

998
01:09:23,083 --> 01:09:25,208
After that, pick out your favorite toy,

999
01:09:25,291 --> 01:09:27,500
and, um, I'll be there soon
to join you, okay?

1000
01:09:28,875 --> 01:09:29,833
[Isaura chuckles softly]

1001
01:09:30,375 --> 01:09:31,375
Go have fun.

1002
01:09:31,875 --> 01:09:33,000
Love you both.

1003
01:09:38,250 --> 01:09:42,333
[El Chapo] Stop being irresponsible.
Think about the future of your kids.

1004
01:09:43,458 --> 01:09:46,708
Do you know how many kids
I have? Fucking 18.

1005
01:09:47,958 --> 01:09:51,125
And all of those kids
have everything they could ever need.

1006
01:09:51,208 --> 01:09:52,291
You know why?

1007
01:09:52,375 --> 01:09:54,875
It's because I can. Because of money.

1008
01:09:54,958 --> 01:09:55,958
And with that money,

1009
01:09:56,041 --> 01:09:59,791
I also provide for the countless kids
who were born with a gun in their hands

1010
01:09:59,875 --> 01:10:01,250
instead of a bottle to drink.

1011
01:10:01,333 --> 01:10:02,791
There's a shitload of those kids.

1012
01:10:04,791 --> 01:10:07,500
Well, I'm not saying that I don't think
you've been a good provider.

1013
01:10:08,958 --> 01:10:11,291
But those kids
that you claim to be helping?

1014
01:10:13,875 --> 01:10:15,833
They're all just living on their knees.

1015
01:10:16,541 --> 01:10:18,000
But they eat because of me.

1016
01:10:18,083 --> 01:10:19,583
Right. You feed them.

1017
01:10:22,916 --> 01:10:24,375
Then you make them kill.

1018
01:10:26,125 --> 01:10:27,291
Then they end up dead.

1019
01:10:27,375 --> 01:10:28,666
Ah, <i>chingá!</i>

1020
01:10:29,166 --> 01:10:31,083
Don't policemen kill people too?

1021
01:10:31,166 --> 01:10:33,541
Pretty much the same
if you think about it.

1022
01:10:33,625 --> 01:10:35,541
The only difference
between your men and mine

1023
01:10:35,625 --> 01:10:38,416
is that you guys
barely have enough to get by,

1024
01:10:38,500 --> 01:10:40,833
and my men can't spend it fast enough.

1025
01:10:41,666 --> 01:10:42,541
Huh.

1026
01:10:45,000 --> 01:10:46,500
Doesn't sound too bad.

1027
01:10:47,333 --> 01:10:48,333
[El Chapo] So, Carmona,

1028
01:10:49,916 --> 01:10:51,625
how many people have you killed?

1029
01:10:52,125 --> 01:10:54,125
[distant helicopters approaching]

1030
01:11:02,250 --> 01:11:04,416
[tense music playing]

1031
01:11:13,166 --> 01:11:15,708
Enough, <i>cabrón!</i>
Get me the fuck out of here! Come on!

1032
01:11:16,916 --> 01:11:19,333
Can't you just tell me
what the fuck you want, <i>cabrón?!</i>

1033
01:11:19,416 --> 01:11:22,625
-Ask for whatever you want, <i>puto!</i>
-[Arturo] Sit down. Fucking sit!

1034
01:11:22,708 --> 01:11:24,708
-[El Chapo] Don't be a fucking--
-Sit your ass down!

1035
01:11:35,166 --> 01:11:36,291
[El Cholo] Listen, Officer.

1036
01:11:36,875 --> 01:11:39,541
I know I'm fucked,
and the boss might be fucked, too,

1037
01:11:40,041 --> 01:11:42,666
but don't forget
about how this is gonna play out for you.

1038
01:11:42,750 --> 01:11:46,125
I'm gonna murder your entire family,
one by one, in front of you, <i>cabrón.</i>

1039
01:11:47,416 --> 01:11:49,208
You really think anyone has your back?

1040
01:11:49,708 --> 01:11:52,333
No one's gonna save you.
You're on your own!

1041
01:11:53,083 --> 01:11:54,458
Go fuck yourself.

1042
01:11:54,541 --> 01:11:55,916
You can put me in a fucking prison,

1043
01:11:56,000 --> 01:11:58,375
but once I get in,
I'm gonna put a million on your head.

1044
01:12:01,416 --> 01:12:03,375
What makes you think
you'll actually make it there?

1045
01:12:04,625 --> 01:12:05,708
Who knows you're here?

1046
01:12:06,208 --> 01:12:07,500
It's only me.

1047
01:12:08,208 --> 01:12:11,666
And you have no fucking idea
how much I wanna blow your brains out.

1048
01:12:12,166 --> 01:12:15,083
So just keep mouthing off, and you'll--

1049
01:12:20,250 --> 01:12:22,541
Took you guys long enough.
Where the hell were you?

1050
01:12:22,625 --> 01:12:25,708
[man] This is Commander Carmona's
patrol car, right?

1051
01:12:26,250 --> 01:12:28,500
[breathes shakily]

1052
01:12:29,708 --> 01:12:31,083
[man] Answer me, <i>cabrón!</i>

1053
01:12:32,875 --> 01:12:35,916
They were able
to get the boss too! El Chapo!

1054
01:12:39,750 --> 01:12:40,583
Rosales?

1055
01:12:41,750 --> 01:12:43,625
The fuck are you doing
all the way out here?

1056
01:12:43,708 --> 01:12:44,625
Barraza?

1057
01:12:44,708 --> 01:12:45,791
Yes, dumbass!

1058
01:12:46,291 --> 01:12:47,208
[exhales]

1059
01:12:51,166 --> 01:12:52,791
<i>Pinche, </i>Barraza!

1060
01:12:53,291 --> 01:12:55,458
Jesus, you scared the shit outta me, man.

1061
01:12:55,958 --> 01:12:58,416
So wait, how long you been in Mochis?

1062
01:12:58,500 --> 01:13:00,416
[chuckles wryly] Three days, <i>cabrón.</i>

1063
01:13:00,500 --> 01:13:01,416
[Barraza chuckles]

1064
01:13:01,500 --> 01:13:02,916
-Fuck!
-And you?

1065
01:13:03,541 --> 01:13:06,000
Man, it smells
like you haven't showered in weeks.

1066
01:13:06,500 --> 01:13:08,208
Shit, that's because I've been undercover.

1067
01:13:08,291 --> 01:13:11,208
Well, you guys are fucking precious, yeah?
Enough with the fucking reunion!

1068
01:13:13,750 --> 01:13:15,666
What the hell do we do, <i>cabrón?</i>

1069
01:13:16,375 --> 01:13:18,291
If his men get here before ours do,

1070
01:13:18,833 --> 01:13:20,333
we might as well be dead, <i>guey.</i>

1071
01:13:21,500 --> 01:13:22,916
We'll be ready.

1072
01:13:25,291 --> 01:13:26,500
-Good luck.
-Yeah.

1073
01:13:27,000 --> 01:13:29,000
[helicopter blades whirring]

1074
01:13:29,916 --> 01:13:31,916
[suspenseful music playing]

1075
01:13:35,958 --> 01:13:38,916
Okay, marine, don't lose him now.
Keep close.

1076
01:13:42,833 --> 01:13:44,041
Goddamn it!

1077
01:13:45,041 --> 01:13:47,458
We gotta lose those motherfuckers
before we get to the motel.

1078
01:13:48,875 --> 01:13:50,833
[man 1] Step on it, man.
They're right on our ass!

1079
01:14:02,708 --> 01:14:03,625
Get ready, Foco.

1080
01:14:04,708 --> 01:14:06,500
The shitstorm's about to begin.

1081
01:14:08,875 --> 01:14:13,041
Fuck it, stop the car, man. Let's just
fucking square up with these marines.

1082
01:14:15,541 --> 01:14:17,250
Stick with them. We're close.

1083
01:14:17,333 --> 01:14:20,000
-[man 2] Are you sure, boss?
-Stop the damn car.

1084
01:14:21,083 --> 01:14:21,916
Okay, sir.

1085
01:14:25,583 --> 01:14:28,750
-What's up, assholes? Fucking want some?!
-Take cover!

1086
01:14:28,833 --> 01:14:32,000
I swear to God,
I'm gonna kill all you motherfuckers!

1087
01:14:32,083 --> 01:14:33,916
-[marine 1] Take cover!
-[Foco] Get down!

1088
01:14:34,000 --> 01:14:36,208
Come at me, assholes!
Suck my fucking dick!

1089
01:14:36,291 --> 01:14:38,750
-[marine 2 groans]
-I got you. Stay down!

1090
01:14:39,666 --> 01:14:41,541
Press forward when they reload!

1091
01:14:41,625 --> 01:14:44,625
I'm gonna cut your heads off,
<i>hijos de puta!</i>

1092
01:14:46,291 --> 01:14:48,916
-Foco, Vaquero, move in, left flank!
-Sir!

1093
01:14:49,000 --> 01:14:50,250
Reload!

1094
01:14:50,791 --> 01:14:52,000
Puma, Black Charro! On me!

1095
01:14:53,750 --> 01:14:55,875
-Fuck.
-[man 1] Fuck you, pigs!

1096
01:14:57,000 --> 01:14:58,666
Counterattack! Go!

1097
01:15:05,500 --> 01:15:06,916
[tense music playing]

1098
01:15:09,541 --> 01:15:10,958
Fuck you, jarheads!

1099
01:15:11,875 --> 01:15:12,791
[vice admiral] Grenade!

1100
01:15:13,291 --> 01:15:15,000
[groaning]

1101
01:15:18,583 --> 01:15:19,541
[music fades]

1102
01:15:21,208 --> 01:15:24,291
You're not gonna get anything
for turning me in, Carmona.

1103
01:15:25,583 --> 01:15:27,250
And you'll be fucked if you do.

1104
01:15:27,791 --> 01:15:30,000
Come on. You know how it is over there.

1105
01:15:30,083 --> 01:15:34,125
The government or the DEA
will make you and your family disappear.

1106
01:15:34,208 --> 01:15:37,791
Because then they can blame it on me,
and give me a longer sentence.

1107
01:15:37,875 --> 01:15:39,166
'Cause that's what they do.

1108
01:15:39,250 --> 01:15:40,958
You know I'm right.

1109
01:15:41,541 --> 01:15:44,416
Listen, I'm giving you my word.

1110
01:15:46,041 --> 01:15:48,791
Just take me to Che Ríos
and I'll give you ten million.

1111
01:15:48,875 --> 01:15:50,125
Fifteen.

1112
01:15:53,083 --> 01:15:54,166
You promised 15.

1113
01:15:54,250 --> 01:15:55,375
Ah, that was before.

1114
01:15:55,458 --> 01:15:57,625
But if we get there today, I promise you,

1115
01:15:58,125 --> 01:16:01,000
I'll have my men waiting there
with ten million in cash.

1116
01:16:03,291 --> 01:16:05,250
You think you can buy me off?

1117
01:16:07,375 --> 01:16:08,333
Not me.

1118
01:16:10,208 --> 01:16:12,333
You don't have all of us in your pocket.

1119
01:16:17,125 --> 01:16:20,041
You think you're a good person,
like you're a saint, don't you?

1120
01:16:22,250 --> 01:16:24,916
I had to kill a kid
who was selling your shit,

1121
01:16:25,833 --> 01:16:28,291
and two innocent people died that day.

1122
01:16:30,041 --> 01:16:31,458
Because we're at war.

1123
01:16:33,666 --> 01:16:37,500
And civilians end up dying as collateral
in the crossfire.

1124
01:16:38,166 --> 01:16:42,041
Because of people like you,
who murder and poison society.

1125
01:16:42,541 --> 01:16:45,625
I don't understand how someone like you
can even sleep at night.

1126
01:16:46,333 --> 01:16:47,500
Seriously.

1127
01:16:49,000 --> 01:16:51,916
And you think that if you just keep
building chapels you're forgiven?

1128
01:16:52,000 --> 01:16:53,166
Fuck off!

1129
01:16:54,958 --> 01:16:58,333
I can't wait to put you away
so I can watch you rot in that cell.

1130
01:17:02,416 --> 01:17:04,250
But if I can't put you in jail…

1131
01:17:07,166 --> 01:17:08,500
then I'll put you in the ground.

1132
01:17:09,000 --> 01:17:10,291
[tense music sting]

1133
01:17:25,458 --> 01:17:26,625
[vehicle approaching]

1134
01:17:26,708 --> 01:17:27,791
[distant thud]

1135
01:17:43,625 --> 01:17:45,625
[tense music playing]

1136
01:17:46,625 --> 01:17:47,666
The girls.

1137
01:17:50,291 --> 01:17:51,458
[man 1] Come on, move it!

1138
01:17:52,791 --> 01:17:54,000
-[gasps]
-[Joana] Is that Papa?

1139
01:17:54,083 --> 01:17:55,875
[Elízabeth] What's wrong? Who's outside?

1140
01:17:55,958 --> 01:17:58,250
-[Isaura] Come here. Shh.
-[Joana] I'm getting scared, mama.

1141
01:17:58,333 --> 01:18:00,666
Don't worry, girls.
Dad will be here soon, I promise.

1142
01:18:00,750 --> 01:18:03,583
-Who's outside?
-Shh, shh. Let's lower our voices.

1143
01:18:03,666 --> 01:18:05,416
-We're gonna be fine.
-[Elízabeth] I'm scared.

1144
01:18:05,500 --> 01:18:07,083
-[Isaura] Shh.
-[Elízabeth] Where is Papa?

1145
01:18:07,166 --> 01:18:08,833
TWO TRUCKS FULL OF HITMEN
CAME TO THE HOUSE.

1146
01:18:08,916 --> 01:18:10,291
[Isaura] Answer me, Arturo.

1147
01:18:10,375 --> 01:18:11,833
THE THREE OF US ARE HERE.

1148
01:18:11,916 --> 01:18:13,875
[cell phone chimes]

1149
01:18:20,500 --> 01:18:22,250
[tense music playing]

1150
01:18:24,333 --> 01:18:25,833
[breathes shakily]

1151
01:18:25,916 --> 01:18:27,000
This can't be happening.

1152
01:18:30,333 --> 01:18:32,333
[cell phone dialing]

1153
01:18:35,000 --> 01:18:36,083
-Where's Papa?
-Arturo!

1154
01:18:36,166 --> 01:18:37,166
Isa!

1155
01:18:37,250 --> 01:18:39,791
Arturo, there are two trucks outside
and they're--

1156
01:18:39,875 --> 01:18:41,500
[screams]

1157
01:18:41,583 --> 01:18:42,541
Hey!

1158
01:18:42,625 --> 01:18:43,958
No! Please, please, don't shoot!.

1159
01:18:44,041 --> 01:18:46,208
You assholes get the fuck out of my house!

1160
01:18:46,291 --> 01:18:48,500
-Please, sir, please!
-Who are they, Mama?

1161
01:18:48,583 --> 01:18:50,166
Leave them alone!

1162
01:18:50,250 --> 01:18:52,666
Sounds like they already made it inside.

1163
01:18:52,750 --> 01:18:54,416
[panicked breathing on phone]

1164
01:18:54,500 --> 01:18:55,416
[Isaura] <i>Please!</i>

1165
01:18:56,291 --> 01:18:57,875
<i>Please don't kill us!</i>

1166
01:18:57,958 --> 01:18:59,083
Tell them to stand down.

1167
01:18:59,166 --> 01:19:00,416
Tell them to back off!

1168
01:19:00,500 --> 01:19:01,916
[Isaura] <i>No! Please, please!</i>

1169
01:19:02,000 --> 01:19:04,333
Say it! Tell your guys to let them go!

1170
01:19:05,916 --> 01:19:07,916
[vehicle approaching]

1171
01:19:08,666 --> 01:19:09,625
[Isaura] <i>Please!</i>

1172
01:19:11,416 --> 01:19:13,458
How did you think this was going to end?

1173
01:19:13,541 --> 01:19:14,666
[Joana] <i>Mama, I'm scared.</i>

1174
01:19:14,750 --> 01:19:18,500
[El Chapo] I told you. This is what
you get for playing the hero, <i>cabrón.</i>

1175
01:19:19,291 --> 01:19:22,125
They're my daughters, man.
They're just little kids!

1176
01:19:22,208 --> 01:19:23,458
[Isaura] <i>No, don't shoot!</i>

1177
01:19:23,541 --> 01:19:25,708
-They're gonna keep screaming for help.
-[Isaura] <i>Please!</i>

1178
01:19:25,791 --> 01:19:27,333
And there's nothing you can do.

1179
01:19:27,916 --> 01:19:29,916
[suspenseful music playing]

1180
01:19:30,708 --> 01:19:32,708
[indistinct clamoring on phone]

1181
01:19:34,833 --> 01:19:35,958
-[Isaura] <i>Please!</i>
-Isa!

1182
01:19:36,541 --> 01:19:38,416
-[crying on phone]
-Isa, are you there?

1183
01:19:38,500 --> 01:19:40,250
-[Isaura] Please!
-[Elízabeth cries]

1184
01:19:40,333 --> 01:19:42,041
We didn't do anything.

1185
01:19:42,125 --> 01:19:43,333
Are you there?

1186
01:19:43,416 --> 01:19:46,958
Shush. Please don't hurt them!
They're just kids, so please don't.

1187
01:19:47,041 --> 01:19:48,083
-Can you--
-[gunshot]

1188
01:19:48,166 --> 01:19:50,041
[silence]

1189
01:19:50,125 --> 01:19:52,125
[breathing shakily]

1190
01:20:01,666 --> 01:20:04,125
Now I'm going
to fucking kill you, motherfucker!

1191
01:20:04,625 --> 01:20:06,500
[vice admiral] Drop your gun, Officer!

1192
01:20:07,708 --> 01:20:08,958
You're fucking dead, <i>puto!</i>

1193
01:20:09,041 --> 01:20:12,000
-I need you to calm down, Officer!
-I'm gonna fucking blow your brains out!

1194
01:20:13,000 --> 01:20:15,916
Stand down! I'm giving you an order
as the vice admiral!

1195
01:20:16,000 --> 01:20:18,083
I swear I'm gonna
fucking blow your brains out!

1196
01:20:18,166 --> 01:20:19,416
[marine] Put it down, Officer.

1197
01:20:20,250 --> 01:20:21,333
[screams]

1198
01:20:21,416 --> 01:20:23,708
[cell phone buzzing and ringing]

1199
01:20:30,666 --> 01:20:31,500
[exhales]

1200
01:20:41,375 --> 01:20:44,541
[Isaura breathes shakily]
<i>Arturo! We're okay.</i>

1201
01:20:45,041 --> 01:20:46,375
[cries]

1202
01:20:46,458 --> 01:20:48,750
[haunting music playing]

1203
01:20:51,583 --> 01:20:52,583
[gunshot]

1204
01:20:55,000 --> 01:20:57,375
[screams] Don't look!

1205
01:20:57,458 --> 01:20:59,000
[crying]

1206
01:21:04,416 --> 01:21:06,833
The… The Army got to us. We're okay.

1207
01:21:06,916 --> 01:21:08,916
[breathing shakily]

1208
01:21:20,958 --> 01:21:23,458
Your six-month vacation is over, Chapo.

1209
01:21:24,166 --> 01:21:25,000
Yeah.

1210
01:21:26,666 --> 01:21:27,541
I'm done.

1211
01:21:33,625 --> 01:21:34,875
Piece of shit!

1212
01:21:35,375 --> 01:21:38,125
Okay, okay, you got him. Now relax.

1213
01:21:39,458 --> 01:21:40,458
Escort him out.

1214
01:21:40,958 --> 01:21:43,041
Let me go. Don't touch me.

1215
01:21:45,708 --> 01:21:46,708
Marines!

1216
01:21:47,208 --> 01:21:48,291
[El Chapo groans quietly]

1217
01:21:50,333 --> 01:21:54,041
At this moment, you are at the disposal
of the Mexican Naval Forces.

1218
01:21:55,166 --> 01:21:57,166
I got your buddy waiting for you.

1219
01:21:58,083 --> 01:21:59,875
That is, if he's still alive.

1220
01:22:01,166 --> 01:22:02,250
[marine] Orders, sir?

1221
01:22:03,416 --> 01:22:04,541
[vice admiral] Bring him out!

1222
01:22:04,625 --> 01:22:06,625
[tense music playing]

1223
01:22:12,625 --> 01:22:14,958
[soldier] Mexican Army! Surrender!

1224
01:22:15,458 --> 01:22:17,625
Hurry up! Everyone, on the ground!

1225
01:22:17,708 --> 01:22:19,916
Hands behind your head.
Give us your weapons!

1226
01:22:20,416 --> 01:22:21,958
Come on, hurry up! All of you!

1227
01:22:22,041 --> 01:22:24,041
[sirens wail]

1228
01:22:26,750 --> 01:22:29,708
-[man 1] Keep that clear.
-[man 2] Two over there, three over here.

1229
01:22:33,833 --> 01:22:35,291
We got you guys a present.

1230
01:22:36,625 --> 01:22:37,750
Rot in hell.

1231
01:22:39,000 --> 01:22:40,333
[man 2] All right, copy that.

1232
01:22:42,750 --> 01:22:45,000
-[Valladares] Are you okay?
-I'm fine, sir.

1233
01:22:47,208 --> 01:22:48,166
Well done, Carmona.

1234
01:22:48,958 --> 01:22:50,333
You've nothing to worry about.

1235
01:22:50,416 --> 01:22:53,458
Your family and your house
will be under the protection of the Army.

1236
01:22:54,208 --> 01:22:56,125
-Thanks.
-[vice admiral] Hello, gentlemen.

1237
01:22:57,250 --> 01:22:58,916
Vice Admiral Ortega.

1238
01:22:59,666 --> 01:23:02,166
Officers, thanks for your cooperation.

1239
01:23:03,000 --> 01:23:04,083
Commissioner,

1240
01:23:05,083 --> 01:23:08,208
get your men out of here
as soon as possible. For your own safety.

1241
01:23:08,708 --> 01:23:12,083
From this point on, the Navy
will take these two into their custody.

1242
01:23:20,625 --> 01:23:21,541
What are you doing?

1243
01:23:21,625 --> 01:23:24,333
[man 1] Stand down!
Stand down. Hold your fire.

1244
01:23:24,416 --> 01:23:27,125
-[man 2] Put your fucking guns down!
-[man 1] Hold fire. Stand down.

1245
01:23:27,208 --> 01:23:28,208
[man 3] Hold your fire.

1246
01:23:28,291 --> 01:23:30,625
-[man 1] Soldier.
-[man 2] Put your guns down!

1247
01:23:30,708 --> 01:23:32,458
-[man 1] Relax!
-[man 3] Come on.

1248
01:23:32,958 --> 01:23:36,791
It was the Federal Police, not the Navy,
who captured Joaquin Guzmán.

1249
01:23:37,458 --> 01:23:40,833
So we're all gonna go together
to the presidential hangar to report it.

1250
01:23:40,916 --> 01:23:41,916
Are we clear?

1251
01:23:50,916 --> 01:23:51,833
Marines!

1252
01:23:51,916 --> 01:23:53,166
[marines] Yes, sir!

1253
01:23:54,458 --> 01:23:55,916
Put your weapons down!

1254
01:23:56,000 --> 01:23:57,083
[marines] Yes, sir!

1255
01:23:57,708 --> 01:24:00,166
<i>Federales, </i>lower your weapons!

1256
01:24:00,250 --> 01:24:02,541
[poignant music playing]

1257
01:24:02,625 --> 01:24:04,541
-Marines!
-[marines] Yes, sir!

1258
01:24:04,625 --> 01:24:06,541
-Escort them out!
-[marines] Yes, sir!

1259
01:24:10,625 --> 01:24:12,000
[Valladares] Well done, boys.

1260
01:24:12,083 --> 01:24:14,083
[helicopter blades whirring]

1261
01:24:22,750 --> 01:24:29,583
{\an8}JANUARY 8, 2016 10:32 AM
LOS MOCHIS, SINALOA

1262
01:24:50,250 --> 01:24:51,166
You good?

1263
01:24:51,791 --> 01:24:52,916
Yeah, I'm good.

1264
01:24:53,958 --> 01:24:56,833
Those marine assholes
were trying to take all of the credit.

1265
01:24:56,916 --> 01:25:00,000
Doesn't matter to me
who takes the credit for it.

1266
01:25:02,666 --> 01:25:05,125
I just worry about the Army
keeping their word to us.

1267
01:25:05,208 --> 01:25:08,000
No, don't say that, Carmona.
They'll protect us.

1268
01:25:08,500 --> 01:25:10,333
I'm a year from retirement, man.

1269
01:25:11,250 --> 01:25:12,291
[scoffs]

1270
01:25:12,375 --> 01:25:13,375
<i>Cabrón.</i>

1271
01:25:15,375 --> 01:25:18,500
-The hell are you doing here?
-I could ask you the same thing.

1272
01:25:19,000 --> 01:25:20,708
I can't believe you're here, <i>cabrón.</i>

1273
01:25:21,458 --> 01:25:23,250
What a fucking mess you two got into.

1274
01:25:23,958 --> 01:25:25,500
You actually got El Chapo!

1275
01:25:26,291 --> 01:25:27,208
Fucking crazy.

1276
01:25:27,791 --> 01:25:31,583
Well, my boy Barraza here,
thanks to him, we got El Cholo.

1277
01:25:33,083 --> 01:25:34,291
Well, thanks then.

1278
01:25:34,375 --> 01:25:35,583
Any time.

1279
01:25:35,666 --> 01:25:38,041
Well, I've got somebody
waiting for me, huh?

1280
01:25:38,125 --> 01:25:39,583
[both chuckle]

1281
01:25:40,166 --> 01:25:41,333
Go get her, man!

1282
01:25:47,125 --> 01:25:48,708
-Sheesh.
-<i>Cabrón.</i>

1283
01:25:50,875 --> 01:25:52,458
-Glad you're my partner.
-Me too.

1284
01:25:52,541 --> 01:25:53,625
Thank you.

1285
01:25:56,166 --> 01:25:58,666
-We're fucking idiots, aren't we?
-Oh, complete idiots.

1286
01:25:58,750 --> 01:26:00,041
[both chuckle]

1287
01:26:03,958 --> 01:26:09,750
IN JULY 2019, JOAQUÍN GUZMÁN LOERA
WAS SENTENCED TO LIFE PLUS 30 YEARS.

1288
01:26:10,541 --> 01:26:14,041
"EL CHOLO" IVÁN GASTÉLUM
WAS EXTRADITED TO THE USA

1289
01:26:14,125 --> 01:26:18,000
FOR DRUG TRAFFICKING AND FIREARM CRIMES.

1290
01:26:21,000 --> 01:26:22,708
CARMONA WAS PROMOTED
AND COMMENDED.

1291
01:26:22,791 --> 01:26:24,833
HE WAS ASSIGNED
TO A SECURITY DETAIL OVERSEAS.

1292
01:26:24,916 --> 01:26:27,041
CARMONA AND HIS FAMILY
THEN RETURNED TO MEXICO.

1293
01:26:27,125 --> 01:26:29,000
HIS WHEREABOUTS
AND IDENTITY REMAIN CLASSIFIED.

1294
01:26:31,416 --> 01:26:33,250
HÉCTOR ROSALES WAS DECORATED
FOR HIS BRAVERY

1295
01:26:33,333 --> 01:26:34,958
AND ASSIGNED OVERSEAS WITH CARMONA.

1296
01:26:35,041 --> 01:26:36,833
HE DECIDED TO POSTPONE HIS RETIREMENT.

1297
01:26:36,916 --> 01:26:39,250
HIS WHEREABOUTS
AND IDENTITY REMAIN CLASSIFIED.

1298
01:26:39,333 --> 01:26:41,333
[poignant music continues]

1299
01:27:54,166 --> 01:27:56,166
[tense music playing]

1300
01:30:59,500 --> 01:31:00,416
[music fades]

